event: values
data: {"messages":[{"content":"请分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"34ad83b1-a1de-4e51-bbd5-2b2fe8512eb1"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze-video</name>\n      <description>专业视频抽帧与取证准备技能。支持场景检测、多阶段帧提取和 metadata 生成，供 single-video-event-analysis 做 LLM 审帧使用；本 skill 不再作为最终事件检测入口。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/analyze-video/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>batch-video-ingestion</name>\n      <description>Batch ingest local monitoring videos into the Elasticsearch video library after city-video-intelligence has routed the request, with metadata, sampled-frame object summaries, and searchable documents. For direct user video ingestion, ingest-and-embed, Elasticsearch, StreetModel, or business video-library requests, load city-video-intelligence first. Use this atomic skill when Codex already has a clear ingestion plan, video directory, video manifest, camera_id, or multiple video files to index for later retrieval and statistics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/batch-video-ingestion/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>camera-health-check</name>\n      <description>Check video monitoring camera quality from sampled frames and return health status before downstream event generation. Use when Codex has camera_id and frames and needs to gate or downgrade event confidence for offline, unavailable, degraded, black-screen, blurred, occluded, frozen, corrupted, or shifted camera feeds.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/camera-health-check/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>city-video-intelligence</name>\n      <description>Business orchestration for city video intelligence requests. Use when users ask for monitoring video search, semantic video retrieval, event review, object statistics, evidence packages, video ingestion, camera health operations, cross-camera analysis, or role-based scenarios such as traffic police, property security, urban management, emergency management, or legal evidence preparation. Also use it when the user asks what the current data and skills can or cannot support (capability-boundary questions) — it answers with an explicit capability_gap instead of guessing. This skill maps business intent to existing custom video skills and prevents ad hoc code generation unless the user explicitly asks for development or testing.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>duplicate-event-merge</name>\n      <description>Merge duplicate video event candidates from the same camera, event type, ROI, evidence frames, or overlapping time window. Use after single-video-event-analysis or batch video analysis when Codex has a list of Event Candidate records and needs canonical events plus duplicate mappings.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/duplicate-event-merge/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>evidence-package-generation</name>\n      <description>Generate an evidence package manifest for indexed monitoring videos or event/search results, including snapshot evidence and optional short video clips. Use when Codex needs a package_id, manifest URI, evidence items, hashes, and reusable evidence artifacts.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/evidence-package-generation/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>evidence-snapshot</name>\n      <description>Generate snapshot evidence for video monitoring event candidates. Use when Codex has an event, event_id, evidence_frame_ids, image_uri, or frame list and needs a snapshot URI, SHA-256 integrity hash, created_at timestamp, privacy masking status, and Evidence schema output.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/evidence-snapshot/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>ffmpeg-utils</name>\n      <description>视频处理工具集，支持视频截取和关键帧提取。常用于将监控视频剪辑为证据片段。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/ffmpeg-utils/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>frame-sampling</name>\n      <description>Sample structured frames from an existing video file. Use when Codex has video_path, file_path, raw_segment_uri, camera_id, sampling_strategy, capture_seconds, or provided frame records and needs stable Frame schema outputs. This skill exposes OpenCV-backed real video frame extraction.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/frame-sampling/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>human-review-routing</name>\n      <description>Decide whether video monitoring event candidates require manual review. Use after event generation and evidence creation when Codex has event confidence, event_type, review_threshold, camera_health, high_risk_event_types, newly added camera signals, or enforcement-impact flags and needs review queue routing.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>object-detection</name>\n      <description>Detect visible objects in sampled video frames and return standard Detection schema only. Use when Codex needs YOLO labels, confidences, and bounding boxes for people, vehicles, or COCO objects. Do not use this skill to infer events, abnormal behavior, accidents, fights, falls, congestion, intrusion, smoke/fire, or business semantics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/object-detection/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>object-statistics</name>\n      <description>Compute object statistics for monitoring videos from Elasticsearch video-library records or local detections/tracks JSON. Use when Codex needs counts by label, camera, time bucket, or movement state.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/object-statistics/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>object-tracking</name>\n      <description>Track detected objects across video frames and return Track schema for object analytics only. Use when Codex has frame-level detections and needs stable track ids, trajectories, duration, last bbox, movement state, confidence, and evidence frame ids. Do not use this skill to infer video events or abnormal behavior.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/object-tracking/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>privacy-masking</name>\n      <description>Mask sensitive visual data in video evidence such as faces, license plates, phone numbers, and doorplates. Use when Codex has an evidence image URI and explicit sensitive_regions bbox coordinates, or privacy_masking config and needs a masked URI before exposing snapshots or clips externally. This skill exposes OpenCV image read/write and Gaussian blur masking for real files.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/privacy-masking/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>roi-mapping</name>\n      <description>Match detections or tracks against configured camera ROI polygons for geometric object analytics. Use when Codex has camera_id plus tracks or objects and needs point containment or bbox overlap matches for configured areas. Do not use this skill to decide event semantics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/roi-mapping/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>single-video-event-analysis</name>\n      <description>Analyze one local monitoring video for incidents after city-video-intelligence has routed the request, by extracting timestamped frames and having the LLM review visible evidence. Use for fight, fall, traffic accident, congestion, crowd gathering, smoke/fire, intrusion, illegal occupation, or other abnormal events. For direct user monitoring-video event questions, load city-video-intelligence first. This skill is the only custom event-detection entrypoint; YOLO/object detection may be used only as optional object context and must not decide event semantics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-embedding-index</name>\n      <description>Generate text embeddings or StreetModel sampled-frame image embeddings for video-library documents after city-video-intelligence has routed the request. Only enrich citybrain-video-library in place. For direct user StreetModel, ingest-and-embed, semantic retrieval, benchmark, or keyword-vs-vector requests, load city-video-intelligence first.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-embedding-index/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-object-analytics</name>\n      <description>Deterministic structured entrypoint for local-video object detection and cross-frame tracking. Use for direct requests to count visible people, vehicles, or other objects, or to track them across frames. The dedicated video_object_analytics tool owns all CLI parameters, model configuration, persistent paths, and downstream skill order.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-object-analytics/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-search</name>\n      <description>Search indexed monitoring videos from text, images, structured filters, or precomputed vectors. Use for keyword retrieval, LLM-optimized text-to-video semantic retrieval, combined keyword/vector search, or image-to-video similarity search against StreetModel/Qwen3-VL video vectors.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-search/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-segment-extraction</name>\n      <description>Extract playable short video evidence clips around event times. Use when Codex has event_id, camera_id, raw_segment_uri, event_time, event_elapsed_seconds, pre_seconds, or post_seconds and needs an MP4 clip URI plus clip time range. This skill exposes FFmpeg-backed clipping for real local videos and memory-backed synthetic clips for tests.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-segment-extraction/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-stream-ingestion</name>\n      <description>Normalize an existing local video file after city-video-intelligence has routed a video-library or analysis request, returning raw segment/session metadata such as duration, resolution, frame rate, codec, and session times. Use it for any \"read this video's duration / resolution / fps / codec / metadata\" or \"turn this video into a standard analysis input\" request instead of running ffprobe by hand. For direct user ingestion, Elasticsearch, StreetModel, search, statistics, evidence, or camera-health requests, load city-video-intelligence first. Use this atomic skill when Codex already has a clear plan and a local MP4/MOV/AVI/MKV file before frame sampling.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-stream-ingestion/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"b1adea96-db0b-4fa5-b74a-91a2e26e870e"},{"content":"<system_reminder>\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\n<hidden_step source=\"intent_recognition\" title=\"意图识别\">\n改写后的任务：场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance\n识别场景：视频监控 (video_surveillance)；场景模式：single；候选场景：video_surveillance\n任务切分：\n- 请分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。\n任务规划：\n1. 读取/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4视频文件，校验文件元数据与编码格式，按预设帧率执行流媒体解码与关键帧抽样，输出可供下游模型调用的标准化图像序列与对应时间戳映射表。\n2. 基于视频监控场景的行为识别能力，对抽样帧序列应用人体姿态估计与动作分类模型，聚焦“打架”与“摔倒”两类目标特征进行时空关联分析，设定置信度阈值进行初筛，输出包含事件类型、预估起止时间及置信度分数的候选事件清单。\n3. 依据运动轨迹突变程度与连续帧状态一致性规则，对候选事件清单进行二次交叉研判与噪声过滤，明确异常动作判定的关键指标与排除口径，输出经算法复核确认的高置信度事件区间数据集。\n4. 将最终确认的事件区间按时间先后逻辑进行序列化编排，整合事件类型、发生时长、画面关键特征摘要及原始视频溯源链接，生成结构化时间线报告供后续业务调度使用。\n场景任务：\n- video_surveillance: 我将分析/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4中的打架和摔倒情况，并以时间线形式输出结果。；参数：{'视频对象': '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4', '监控目标': '打架、摔倒', '输出形式': '时间线'}\n已提取参数：{'视频对象': '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4', '监控目标': '打架、摔倒', '输出形式': '时间线'}\n任务提示：\n- 提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧\n- 提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等\n- 提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口\n- 提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要\n</hidden_step>\n</system_reminder>","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"todo_routing_guidance","id":"d96bf895-4041-4819-9c0a-9b891870cf3d"},{"content":"这是一个视频监控事件分析任务，我先加载编排技能，然后进行打架/摔倒检测。\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":200,"prompt_tokens":13292,"total_tokens":13492,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":84,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":200},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":13292}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-14a7964f-a96c-99df-8a17-f1e11ac5dcce","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1b-87cf-7ff3-b998-ba08c07981bb-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"invoke_skill","args":{"skill_name":"city-video-intelligence","mode":"prepare","input_envelope":"{\"video_path\": \"/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4\", \"event_types\": [\"fight\", \"fall\"], \"output_format\": \"timeline\"}"},"id":"call_6ca3ad4f27f24339b0460ebf","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":13292,"output_tokens":200,"total_tokens":13492,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":84}}},{"content":"{\n  \"status\": \"prepared\",\n  \"skill_name\": \"city-video-intelligence\",\n  \"input_envelope\": {\n    \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n    \"request_id\": \"95b943f1-f783-4352-8556-7f3398b89bdc\",\n    \"skill_name\": \"city-video-intelligence\",\n    \"scenario\": \"video_surveillance\",\n    \"capability\": \"skill_invocation\",\n    \"query\": {\n      \"raw\": \"<system_reminder>\\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\\n<hidden_step source=\\\"intent_recognition\\\" title=\\\"意图识别\\\">\\n改写后的任务：场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance\\n识别场景：视频监控 (video_surveillance)；场景模式：single；候选场景：video_surveillance\\n任务切分：\\n- 请分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。\\n任务规划：\\n1. 读取/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4视频文件，校验文件元数据与编码格式，按预设帧率执行流媒体解码与关键帧抽样，输出可供下游模型调用的标准化图像序列与对应时间戳映射表。\\n2. 基于视频监控场景的行为识别能力，对抽样帧序列应用人体姿态估计与动作分类模型，聚焦“打架”与“摔倒”两类目标特征进行时空关联分析，设定置信度阈值进行初筛，输出包含事件类型、预估起止时间及置信度分数的候选事件清单。\\n3. 依据运动轨迹突变程度与连续帧状态一致性规则，对候选事件清单进行二次交叉研判与噪声过滤，明确异常动作判定的关键指标与排除口径，输出经算法复核确认的高置信度事件区间数据集。\\n4. 将最终确认的事件区间按时间先后逻辑进行序列化编排，整合事件类型、发生时长、画面关键特征摘要及原始视频溯源链接，生成结构化时间线报告供后续业务调度使用。\\n场景任务：\\n- video_surveillance: 我将分析/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4中的打架和摔倒情况，并以时间线形式输出结果。；参数：{'视频对象': '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4', '监控目标': '打架、摔倒', '输出形式': '时间线'}\\n已提取参数：{'视频对象': '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4', '监控目标': '打架、摔倒', '输出形式': '时间线'}\\n任务提示：\\n- 提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧\\n- 提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等\\n- 提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口\\n- 提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要\\n</hidden_step>\\n</system_reminder>\"\n    },\n    \"inputs\": {\n      \"parameters\": {}\n    },\n    \"routing\": {\n      \"selected_skill\": \"city-video-intelligence\",\n      \"allowed_skills\": [\n        \"analyze-video\",\n        \"batch-video-ingestion\",\n        \"camera-health-check\",\n        \"city-video-intelligence\",\n        \"duplicate-event-merge\",\n        \"evidence-package-generation\",\n        \"evidence-snapshot\",\n        \"ffmpeg-utils\",\n        \"frame-sampling\",\n        \"human-review-routing\",\n        \"object-detection\",\n        \"object-statistics\",\n        \"object-tracking\",\n        \"privacy-masking\",\n        \"roi-mapping\",\n        \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n        \"video-embedding-index\",\n        \"video-object-analytics\",\n        \"video-search\",\n        \"video-segment-extraction\",\n        \"video-stream-ingestion\"\n      ],\n      \"selection_owner\": \"lead_agent\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"legacy_invocation\": {\n    \"skill_dir\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence\",\n    \"skill_file\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence/SKILL.md\",\n    \"container_skill_file\": \"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence/SKILL.md\",\n    \"selected_data_sources\": [],\n    \"argv\": [],\n    \"env\": {},\n    \"parameters\": {},\n    \"working_directory\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence\",\n    \"adapter_note\": \"Load the returned container_skill_file, follow its SKILL.md workflow, and use selected_data_sources/parameters as the legacy inputs.\"\n  },\n  \"next_steps\": [\n    \"Read container_skill_file before executing the Skill workflow.\",\n    \"Use selected_data_sources and parameters as the legacy inputs.\",\n    \"After execution, call invoke_skill again with mode='wrap_output' to produce SkillResult.\"\n  ]\n}","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"invoke_skill","id":"869d54da-5978-4a9f-b33f-faa495d3dc00","tool_call_id":"call_6ca3ad4f27f24339b0460ebf","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":83,"prompt_tokens":14617,"total_tokens":14700,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":17,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":83},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":14617}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-99326868-af9b-9ea0-8d5c-05e40f6c0906","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1b-fd44-7e62-bfa0-cfcd3b7acf64-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"description":"读取 city-video-intelligence 技能的工作流说明","path":"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence/SKILL.md"},"id":"call_c80253603ab54078a911657d","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":14617,"output_tokens":83,"total_tokens":14700,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":17}}},{"content":"---\nname: city-video-intelligence\ndescription: Business orchestration for city video intelligence requests. Use when users ask for monitoring video search, semantic video retrieval, event review, object statistics, evidence packages, video ingestion, camera health operations, cross-camera analysis, or role-based scenarios such as traffic police, property security, urban management, emergency management, or legal evidence preparation. Also use it when the user asks what the current data and skills can or cannot support (capability-boundary questions) — it answers with an explicit capability_gap instead of guessing. This skill maps business intent to existing custom video skills and prevents ad hoc code generation unless the user explicitly asks for development or testing.\n---\n\n# City Video Intelligence Orchestration\n\n## Overview\n\nUse this skill as the business layer above the existing video-monitoring atomic skills. It classifies a user request, selects the right capability and scenario, returns the recommended skill chain, and states the expected business deliverable. Use it for direct user tasks as well as planning questions.\n\nThis skill is not a replacement for `video-search`, `single-video-event-analysis`, `object-statistics`, `evidence-package-generation`, `batch-video-ingestion`, `camera-health-check`, or related atomic skills. It tells the agent which of those existing skills to use and when to stop for human confirmation.\n\n## Execution Priority\n\n1. Run `scripts/run.py` with the user's raw request to produce a structured orchestration plan. This is mandatory before any clarification question, except destructive operations that require confirmation.\n2. Read `references/capability-map.md` only when the request is ambiguous, role-based, multi-step, or asks about available capabilities.\n3. Follow the returned `recommended_skill_chain` by loading each downstream skill's `SKILL.md` before running its script.\n4. Return business-facing results: matched capability, scenario, execution plan, deliverables, risks, and required confirmations.\n5. If the plan contains a non-empty `follow_up_question`, stop immediately and make the whole visible response exactly that question as plain assistant text. For ingestion requests, preserve the returned JSON template verbatim. Do not inspect datasets, probe services, load downstream skills, or call `ask_clarification`.\n\n## Atomic CLI\n\n```bash\npython city-video-intelligence/scripts/run.py \\\n  --request \"我是交警队的，需要调取大成路路口今天上午 8-10 点的监控\" \\\n  --output <plan.json>\n```\n\nParameters: `--request`, `--role`, `--output`, `--format`.\n\n## Business Mode Rules\n\n- Do not write ad hoc Python, JavaScript, SQL, or shell code for business requests.\n- Use existing skill scripts and documented workflows. If existing skills cannot satisfy the request, return a `capability_gap` and ask for authorization before implementation work.\n- Treat destructive operations such as deleting indexed videos, rewriting shared indices, or purging test data as requiring explicit confirmation.\n- Treat event conclusions as evidence-bound. If video evidence is missing, blurry, occluded, sparse, or ambiguous, return `requires_human_review=true`.\n- Do not let object detection alone decide event semantics. Use it only as supporting context.\n- For evidence package requests, do not run event analysis merely to invent an event. If the user provides an event time or time range, package that range. If the event time is missing, ask for it or return a plan with the missing input.\n- For development or benchmark requests, use provided test videos, indexes, or query terms. If no test data is available, return `capability_gap` or ask for the missing dataset before running lower-level tools.\n- When asking for missing information, ask only one concrete question. The ingestion-format template returned by the router is the sole exception: show it verbatim. Do not add any text before or after the returned question.\n- If a downstream video skill returns `status: failed`, summarize that failure and stop. Do not debug services or probe ports unless the user explicitly asks for debugging.\n- Attempt StreetModel sampled-frame image embedding for every ingestion request. Always run `video-stream-ingestion`, then `batch-video-ingestion` in metadata-only mode, then `video-embedding-index` with `embedding_provider=streetmodel`, `video_preprocess=image_frames`, and in-place storage. Do not require a StreetModel-visible video mount for the default ingestion path.\n- Store source metadata and StreetModel vector fields in the same `citybrain-video-library` document. Use partial ES updates for embedding enrichment; never replace the full source document with a compact vector copy.\n- Allow video ingestion, search, statistics, evidence lookup, and embedding tools to access only `citybrain-video-library`. Reject every other video index before making an Elasticsearch request.\n- For video search, route image input to direct image-vector retrieval. Route text input to keyword retrieval plus an LLM-optimized text-to-video vector query, then use the search skill's fused ranking.\n- If source ingestion succeeds and vector generation fails, keep the source-index document and return partial success. Report `overall_status=partial_success`, `source_ingestion_status=success`, `vector_status=failed`, and the concrete embedding error. Never roll back or delete the source document.\n- Once the orchestration plan or requested downstream result is available, stop calling tools and summarize the result.\n\n## Capability Families\n\nUse these families to classify requests before selecting downstream skills:\n\n- `video_asset_retrieval`: locate known videos or indexed clips by keyword, camera, place, time, object, or count condition.\n- `semantic_video_retrieval`: retrieve videos by natural-language visual meaning through StreetModel/vector search.\n- `single_video_event_understanding`: inspect one video and produce a timeline, event candidates, confidence, and review status.\n- `object_statistics`: count objects, group by time/camera/type, and summarize trends.\n- `evidence_preservation`: generate snapshots, clips, privacy-masked artifacts, hashes, and package manifests.\n- `video_library_governance`: ingest, index, embed, check storage, or manage video assets.\n- `camera_health_operations`: diagnose online status, black screen, blur, occlusion, freeze, corruption, or view shift.\n- `cross_video_investigation`: compare, correlate, or track across cameras and time windows.\n- `business_scenario_orchestration`: translate role-based requests into one of the above chains.\n- `development_test`: benchmark or compare retrieval/embedding behavior only when the user explicitly asks for testing or development.\n\n## Output Contract\n\nReturn or preserve JSON-compatible fields:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"success\",\n  \"request\": \"\",\n  \"mode\": \"business_operation | development_test\",\n  \"capability\": \"\",\n  \"business_scenario\": \"\",\n  \"recommended_skill_chain\": [],\n  \"execution_plan\": [],\n  \"expected_deliverables\": [],\n  \"embedding_attempt_required\": false,\n  \"embedding_failure_policy\": \"keep_source_and_report_partial_success | null\",\n  \"source_index\": \"citybrain-video-library | null\",\n  \"embedding_target_index\": \"citybrain-video-library | null\",\n  \"embedding_storage_mode\": \"in_place | null\",\n  \"missing_fields\": [],\n  \"follow_up_question\": null,\n  \"guardrails\": [],\n  \"requires_confirmation\": false,\n  \"requires_human_review\": false,\n  \"capability_gap\": null\n}\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Do not execute downstream atomic skills until the plan is clear.\n- Do not create new code to bypass an unsupported operation.\n- Do not perform destructive video-library management without explicit confirmation.\n- Do not produce legal, enforcement, or emergency conclusions without evidence references and review status.\n- For ingestion aggregation, use `success` when source and vector writes succeed, `partial_success` when the source write succeeds but vector generation fails, and `failed` when source ingestion fails.\n- If the plan includes `follow_up_question`, the whole visible response must be exactly that question. Preserve any ingestion JSON template already included in it, but do not append additional preamble, alternatives, or guidance, and do not run downstream tools first.\n- If a plan has `capability_gap`, do not implement new functionality. State the nearest supported workflow or ask the single `follow_up_question` when present.\n","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"read_file","id":"3fc1bf5e-3e54-469b-aa13-5911307f2b15","tool_call_id":"call_c80253603ab54078a911657d","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"先运行编排脚本，获取执行计划：\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":160,"prompt_tokens":16447,"total_tokens":16607,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":34,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":160},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":16447}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-cfb19e7b-f0f1-964c-a605-fa6fcf10b43f","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1c-148a-7711-9080-0323b5ccb7a8-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"bash","args":{"command":"cd /mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence && python scripts/run.py --request \"分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线\" --output /tmp/cvi_plan.json 2>&1","description":"运行 city-video-intelligence 编排脚本获取执行计划"},"id":"call_c14bde36053f4acaaa471be6","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":16447,"output_tokens":160,"total_tokens":16607,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":34}}},{"content":"{\n  \"skill\": \"city-video-intelligence\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"status\": \"success\",\n  \"request\": \"分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线\",\n  \"role\": null,\n  \"mode\": \"business_operation\",\n  \"capability\": \"single_video_event_understanding\",\n  \"capability_label\": \"单视频事件理解\",\n  \"business_scenario\": \"generic_video_intelligence\",\n  \"business_scenario_label\": \"generic_video_intelligence\",\n  \"recommended_skill_chain\": [\n    \"single-video-event-analysis\"\n  ],\n  \"execution_plan\": [\n    {\n      \"step\": \"1\",\n      \"skill\": \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n      \"action\": \"Load single-video-event-analysis and inspect frames for visible event evidence.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"expected_deliverables\": [\n    \"视觉时间线\",\n    \"事件候选\",\n    \"证据帧\",\n    \"置信度\",\n    \"人工复核状态\"\n  ],\n  \"embedding_attempt_required\": false,\n  \"embedding_failure_policy\": null,\n  \"source_index\": null,\n  \"embedding_target_index\": null,\n  \"embedding_storage_mode\": null,\n  \"missing_fields\": [],\n  \"follow_up_question\": null,\n  \"guardrails\": [\n    \"Do not write ad hoc code for this business request.\",\n    \"Load each downstream skill's SKILL.md before executing its script.\",\n    \"Return capability_gap instead of implementing missing functionality.\",\n    \"If follow_up_question is present, stop immediately and make the whole visible response exactly that question.\",\n    \"If a downstream video skill fails, summarize the concrete failure and stop instead of debugging services.\",\n    \"Include evidence references and human-review status for high-risk or enforcement-sensitive conclusions.\"\n  ],\n  \"requires_confirmation\": false,\n  \"requires_human_review\": true,\n  \"capability_gap\": null\n}","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"bash","id":"43cfe2b8-8cef-4d24-a2e4-9aa9be240d5d","tool_call_id":"call_c14bde36053f4acaaa471be6","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"编排计划已确认，需要加载 `single-video-event-analysis` 技能进行事件分析。\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":139,"prompt_tokens":17036,"total_tokens":17175,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":22,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":139},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":17036}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-b59236ba-1049-9d6e-bde4-0a245c06dd5c","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1c-21b0-7121-beb5-1fb87461257b-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"invoke_skill","args":{"input_envelope":"{\"event_types\": [\"fight\", \"fall\"], \"output_format\": \"timeline\", \"video_path\": \"/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4\"}","mode":"prepare","skill_name":"single-video-event-analysis"},"id":"call_8bbdc176c5c340ba90599610","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":17036,"output_tokens":139,"total_tokens":17175,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":22}}},{"content":"{\n  \"status\": \"prepared\",\n  \"skill_name\": \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n  \"input_envelope\": {\n    \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n    \"request_id\": \"7e5b647d-d87f-4d03-a927-e4d6760e0dd0\",\n    \"skill_name\": \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n    \"scenario\": \"video_surveillance\",\n    \"capability\": \"skill_invocation\",\n    \"query\": {\n      \"raw\": \"<system_reminder>\\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\\n<hidden_step source=\\\"intent_recognition\\\" title=\\\"意图识别\\\">\\n改写后的任务：场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance\\n识别场景：视频监控 (video_surveillance)；场景模式：single；候选场景：video_surveillance\\n任务切分：\\n- 请分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。\\n任务规划：\\n1. 读取/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4视频文件，校验文件元数据与编码格式，按预设帧率执行流媒体解码与关键帧抽样，输出可供下游模型调用的标准化图像序列与对应时间戳映射表。\\n2. 基于视频监控场景的行为识别能力，对抽样帧序列应用人体姿态估计与动作分类模型，聚焦“打架”与“摔倒”两类目标特征进行时空关联分析，设定置信度阈值进行初筛，输出包含事件类型、预估起止时间及置信度分数的候选事件清单。\\n3. 依据运动轨迹突变程度与连续帧状态一致性规则，对候选事件清单进行二次交叉研判与噪声过滤，明确异常动作判定的关键指标与排除口径，输出经算法复核确认的高置信度事件区间数据集。\\n4. 将最终确认的事件区间按时间先后逻辑进行序列化编排，整合事件类型、发生时长、画面关键特征摘要及原始视频溯源链接，生成结构化时间线报告供后续业务调度使用。\\n场景任务：\\n- video_surveillance: 我将分析/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4中的打架和摔倒情况，并以时间线形式输出结果。；参数：{'视频对象': '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4', '监控目标': '打架、摔倒', '输出形式': '时间线'}\\n已提取参数：{'视频对象': '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4', '监控目标': '打架、摔倒', '输出形式': '时间线'}\\n任务提示：\\n- 提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧\\n- 提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等\\n- 提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口\\n- 提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要\\n</hidden_step>\\n</system_reminder>\"\n    },\n    \"inputs\": {\n      \"parameters\": {}\n    },\n    \"routing\": {\n      \"selected_skill\": \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n      \"allowed_skills\": [\n        \"analyze-video\",\n        \"batch-video-ingestion\",\n        \"camera-health-check\",\n        \"city-video-intelligence\",\n        \"duplicate-event-merge\",\n        \"evidence-package-generation\",\n        \"evidence-snapshot\",\n        \"ffmpeg-utils\",\n        \"frame-sampling\",\n        \"human-review-routing\",\n        \"object-detection\",\n        \"object-statistics\",\n        \"object-tracking\",\n        \"privacy-masking\",\n        \"roi-mapping\",\n        \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n        \"video-embedding-index\",\n        \"video-object-analytics\",\n        \"video-search\",\n        \"video-segment-extraction\",\n        \"video-stream-ingestion\"\n      ],\n      \"selection_owner\": \"lead_agent\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"legacy_invocation\": {\n    \"skill_dir\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis\",\n    \"skill_file\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis/SKILL.md\",\n    \"container_skill_file\": \"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis/SKILL.md\",\n    \"selected_data_sources\": [],\n    \"argv\": [],\n    \"env\": {},\n    \"parameters\": {},\n    \"working_directory\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis\",\n    \"adapter_note\": \"Load the returned container_skill_file, follow its SKILL.md workflow, and use selected_data_sources/parameters as the legacy inputs.\"\n  },\n  \"next_steps\": [\n    \"Read container_skill_file before executing the Skill workflow.\",\n    \"Use selected_data_sources and parameters as the legacy inputs.\",\n    \"After execution, call invoke_skill again with mode='wrap_output' to produce SkillResult.\"\n  ]\n}","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"invoke_skill","id":"b0148bae-c034-48fe-a3bf-41fc27817f58","tool_call_id":"call_8bbdc176c5c340ba90599610","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":84,"prompt_tokens":18356,"total_tokens":18440,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":19,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":84},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":18356}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-9ce67b55-cff3-99f2-85d3-a7aeb8985d99","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1c-2b40-74b0-aa32-e1126c4daf8c-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"description":"读取 single-video-event-analysis 技能的工作流说明","path":"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis/SKILL.md"},"id":"call_857292050c754af6bc99d80b","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":18356,"output_tokens":84,"total_tokens":18440,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":19}}},{"content":"---\nname: single-video-event-analysis\ndescription: Analyze one local monitoring video for incidents after city-video-intelligence has routed the request, by extracting timestamped frames and having the LLM review visible evidence. Use for fight, fall, traffic accident, congestion, crowd gathering, smoke/fire, intrusion, illegal occupation, or other abnormal events. For direct user monitoring-video event questions, load city-video-intelligence first. This skill is the only custom event-detection entrypoint; YOLO/object detection may be used only as optional object context and must not decide event semantics.\n---\n\n# Single Video Event Analysis\n\n## Purpose\n\nUse this skill when the user wants to know what happened in a monitoring video.\nEvent detection is based on extracted frames and LLM visual review, not YOLO labels,\ntracking duration, ROI geometry, or rule templates alone.\n\n## Business Orchestration Gate\n\nIf this skill is loaded for a direct user monitoring-video request and no `city-video-intelligence` plan has already been executed in the current turn, load `city-video-intelligence` first and run its router script with the raw user request. Continue here only when that plan recommends `single-video-event-analysis`.\n\nDo not edit this skill's files or scripts during business execution. If the script fails, report the concrete failure and stop unless the user explicitly asked for debugging or implementation.\n\n## Execution Priority\n\n1. Use `write_file` to create a small input JSON file, then run `scripts/run.py` with `--input <file>`. Do not use shell heredocs or pass an inline JSON string to `--input`.\n2. Read the returned `review_manifest_uri` and use the listed `frames` as the review set.\n3. Inspect only the listed review frames in chronological order. Default maximum is 8 images.\n4. Read `all_frames_uri` or inspect denser frames only if a reviewed frame visibly suggests a possible event or is too ambiguous to classify.\n5. Produce the final event analysis from visible evidence and stop. Do not keep browsing frames after the conclusion is clear.\n\n## Atomic CLI\n\n```bash\npython single-video-event-analysis/scripts/run.py \\\n  --input <input.json> \\\n  --config <config.json> \\\n  --output <prepared_manifest.json>\n```\n\nUseful fields in `input.json`:\n\n- `video_path`, `file_path`, `raw_segment_uri`, or `video`\n- `camera_id`\n- `target_events`\n- `output_dir`\n- `coarse_fps`, `dense_fps`, `scene_threshold`, `dense_window`, `max_frames`\n\nFor ordinary business questions, omit `max_frames` so the script default samples across the whole video and exposes only 8 review frames. Do not use `max_frames` as the review-image limit. Do not rerun the script after a successful result.\n\n## Review Rules\n\n- Only report events that are visible in the sampled frames.\n- Use `unknown` or `requires_review=true` when evidence is blurry, occluded, sparse, or ambiguous.\n- Use at least two timestamps for temporal claims unless a single frame clearly shows aftermath, smoke, fire, a crash scene, or a fallen person.\n- Do not let YOLO output decide events. YOLO can only provide optional object context such as \"person\", \"car\", or \"truck\".\n- Include negative evidence when useful, such as \"no visible collision before 00:12\".\n- Never include internal thinking markers such as `<think>` or `</think>` in the final user-visible response.\n- If a draft answer contains hidden reasoning before a `</think>` token, discard that hidden text and answer only with the event result and visible evidence summary.\n- For negative findings, phrase the conclusion as evidence-bound, such as \"未在抽样审阅帧中发现交通事故迹象\", unless the reviewed evidence covers the full incident window.\n\n## Output Schema\n\nReturn a JSON-compatible result with:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"video\": {},\n  \"visual_timeline\": [\n    {\n      \"time\": \"00:00:12.000\",\n      \"frame_id\": \"frame_000012000ms\",\n      \"observation\": \"Visible subjects, actions, spatial relations, and scene state.\",\n      \"uncertainty\": \"Optional ambiguity note.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"events\": [\n    {\n      \"event_id\": \"EVT_...\",\n      \"event_type\": \"fight | fall_down | traffic_accident | traffic_congestion | crowd_gathering | smoke_or_fire | intrusion | illegal_occupation | other_abnormal_event | unknown\",\n      \"start_time\": \"00:00:10.000\",\n      \"end_time\": \"00:00:18.000\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.0,\n      \"severity\": \"low | medium | high\",\n      \"evidence_frame_ids\": [],\n      \"reason\": \"Concrete visible evidence and uncertainty.\",\n      \"requires_review\": true\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"Short human-readable summary.\",\n  \"warnings\": []\n}\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Do not call legacy rule-based event skills. They have been removed from this bundle.\n- Do not infer off-camera causes.\n- Do not fabricate exact counts when the frame only supports a range.\n","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"read_file","id":"86a7fa18-c416-43d5-945c-091beacd9334","tool_call_id":"call_857292050c754af6bc99d80b","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"技能已加载。现在创建输入文件并执行分析脚本：\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":133,"prompt_tokens":19580,"total_tokens":19713,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":52,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":133},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":19580}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-9ac8d936-a82f-9161-8b03-09dabb1f1512","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1c-32fb-7ea3-87cd-a06fc3f58e4a-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"bash","args":{"command":"ls -la /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 2>&1","description":"检查视频文件是否存在"},"id":"call_178103da008548158153152c","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":19580,"output_tokens":133,"total_tokens":19713,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":52}}},{"content":"ls: cannot access '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4': No such file or directory","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"bash","id":"032f20c9-8270-4cde-af89-2bed16ce13ff","tool_call_id":"call_178103da008548158153152c","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"视频文件不存在。让我先确认一下上传目录中是否有其他视频文件：\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":142,"prompt_tokens":19700,"total_tokens":19842,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":61,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":142},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":19700}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-f4e16b16-cc05-9e91-ae0b-38dd265cee1f","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1c-3dc6-74a0-8d6b-a79b6e7f4d88-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"bash","args":{"command":"ls -la /mnt/user-data/uploads/ 2>&1 | head -30","description":"检查上传目录中的文件列表"},"id":"call_9e5d310194d54b4fb603364c","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":19700,"output_tokens":142,"total_tokens":19842,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":61}}}],"viewed_images":{},"thread_data":{"workspace_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/eeda22b6-e72a-4ec4-922a-abab62a9f8fd/user-data/workspace","uploads_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/eeda22b6-e72a-4ec4-922a-abab62a9f8fd/user-data/uploads","outputs_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/eeda22b6-e72a-4ec4-922a-abab62a9f8fd/user-data/outputs"},"title":"Surveillance Fight and Fall Timeline","raw_messages":[{"content":"请分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"34ad83b1-a1de-4e51-bbd5-2b2fe8512eb1"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze-video</name>\n      <description>专业视频抽帧与取证准备技能。支持场景检测、多阶段帧提取和 metadata 生成，供 single-video-event-analysis 做 LLM 审帧使用；本 skill 不再作为最终事件检测入口。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/analyze-video/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>batch-video-ingestion</name>\n      <description>Batch ingest local monitoring videos into the Elasticsearch video library after city-video-intelligence has routed the request, with metadata, sampled-frame object summaries, and searchable documents. For direct user video ingestion, ingest-and-embed, Elasticsearch, StreetModel, or business video-library requests, load city-video-intelligence first. Use this atomic skill when Codex already has a clear ingestion plan, video directory, video manifest, camera_id, or multiple video files to index for later retrieval and statistics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/batch-video-ingestion/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>camera-health-check</name>\n      <description>Check video monitoring camera quality from sampled frames and return health status before downstream event generation. Use when Codex has camera_id and frames and needs to gate or downgrade event confidence for offline, unavailable, degraded, black-screen, blurred, occluded, frozen, corrupted, or shifted camera feeds.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/camera-health-check/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>city-video-intelligence</name>\n      <description>Business orchestration for city video intelligence requests. Use when users ask for monitoring video search, semantic video retrieval, event review, object statistics, evidence packages, video ingestion, camera health operations, cross-camera analysis, or role-based scenarios such as traffic police, property security, urban management, emergency management, or legal evidence preparation. Also use it when the user asks what the current data and skills can or cannot support (capability-boundary questions) — it answers with an explicit capability_gap instead of guessing. This skill maps business intent to existing custom video skills and prevents ad hoc code generation unless the user explicitly asks for development or testing.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>duplicate-event-merge</name>\n      <description>Merge duplicate video event candidates from the same camera, event type, ROI, evidence frames, or overlapping time window. Use after single-video-event-analysis or batch video analysis when Codex has a list of Event Candidate records and needs canonical events plus duplicate mappings.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/duplicate-event-merge/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>evidence-package-generation</name>\n      <description>Generate an evidence package manifest for indexed monitoring videos or event/search results, including snapshot evidence and optional short video clips. Use when Codex needs a package_id, manifest URI, evidence items, hashes, and reusable evidence artifacts.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/evidence-package-generation/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>evidence-snapshot</name>\n      <description>Generate snapshot evidence for video monitoring event candidates. Use when Codex has an event, event_id, evidence_frame_ids, image_uri, or frame list and needs a snapshot URI, SHA-256 integrity hash, created_at timestamp, privacy masking status, and Evidence schema output.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/evidence-snapshot/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>ffmpeg-utils</name>\n      <description>视频处理工具集，支持视频截取和关键帧提取。常用于将监控视频剪辑为证据片段。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/ffmpeg-utils/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>frame-sampling</name>\n      <description>Sample structured frames from an existing video file. Use when Codex has video_path, file_path, raw_segment_uri, camera_id, sampling_strategy, capture_seconds, or provided frame records and needs stable Frame schema outputs. This skill exposes OpenCV-backed real video frame extraction.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/frame-sampling/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>human-review-routing</name>\n      <description>Decide whether video monitoring event candidates require manual review. Use after event generation and evidence creation when Codex has event confidence, event_type, review_threshold, camera_health, high_risk_event_types, newly added camera signals, or enforcement-impact flags and needs review queue routing.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>object-detection</name>\n      <description>Detect visible objects in sampled video frames and return standard Detection schema only. Use when Codex needs YOLO labels, confidences, and bounding boxes for people, vehicles, or COCO objects. Do not use this skill to infer events, abnormal behavior, accidents, fights, falls, congestion, intrusion, smoke/fire, or business semantics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/object-detection/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>object-statistics</name>\n      <description>Compute object statistics for monitoring videos from Elasticsearch video-library records or local detections/tracks JSON. Use when Codex needs counts by label, camera, time bucket, or movement state.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/object-statistics/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>object-tracking</name>\n      <description>Track detected objects across video frames and return Track schema for object analytics only. Use when Codex has frame-level detections and needs stable track ids, trajectories, duration, last bbox, movement state, confidence, and evidence frame ids. Do not use this skill to infer video events or abnormal behavior.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/object-tracking/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>privacy-masking</name>\n      <description>Mask sensitive visual data in video evidence such as faces, license plates, phone numbers, and doorplates. Use when Codex has an evidence image URI and explicit sensitive_regions bbox coordinates, or privacy_masking config and needs a masked URI before exposing snapshots or clips externally. This skill exposes OpenCV image read/write and Gaussian blur masking for real files.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/privacy-masking/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>roi-mapping</name>\n      <description>Match detections or tracks against configured camera ROI polygons for geometric object analytics. Use when Codex has camera_id plus tracks or objects and needs point containment or bbox overlap matches for configured areas. Do not use this skill to decide event semantics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/roi-mapping/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>single-video-event-analysis</name>\n      <description>Analyze one local monitoring video for incidents after city-video-intelligence has routed the request, by extracting timestamped frames and having the LLM review visible evidence. Use for fight, fall, traffic accident, congestion, crowd gathering, smoke/fire, intrusion, illegal occupation, or other abnormal events. For direct user monitoring-video event questions, load city-video-intelligence first. This skill is the only custom event-detection entrypoint; YOLO/object detection may be used only as optional object context and must not decide event semantics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-embedding-index</name>\n      <description>Generate text embeddings or StreetModel sampled-frame image embeddings for video-library documents after city-video-intelligence has routed the request. Only enrich citybrain-video-library in place. For direct user StreetModel, ingest-and-embed, semantic retrieval, benchmark, or keyword-vs-vector requests, load city-video-intelligence first.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-embedding-index/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-object-analytics</name>\n      <description>Deterministic structured entrypoint for local-video object detection and cross-frame tracking. Use for direct requests to count visible people, vehicles, or other objects, or to track them across frames. The dedicated video_object_analytics tool owns all CLI parameters, model configuration, persistent paths, and downstream skill order.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-object-analytics/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-search</name>\n      <description>Search indexed monitoring videos from text, images, structured filters, or precomputed vectors. Use for keyword retrieval, LLM-optimized text-to-video semantic retrieval, combined keyword/vector search, or image-to-video similarity search against StreetModel/Qwen3-VL video vectors.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-search/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-segment-extraction</name>\n      <description>Extract playable short video evidence clips around event times. Use when Codex has event_id, camera_id, raw_segment_uri, event_time, event_elapsed_seconds, pre_seconds, or post_seconds and needs an MP4 clip URI plus clip time range. This skill exposes FFmpeg-backed clipping for real local videos and memory-backed synthetic clips for tests.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-segment-extraction/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-stream-ingestion</name>\n      <description>Normalize an existing local video file after city-video-intelligence has routed a video-library or analysis request, returning raw segment/session metadata such as duration, resolution, frame rate, codec, and session times. Use it for any \"read this video's duration / resolution / fps / codec / metadata\" or \"turn this video into a standard analysis input\" request instead of running ffprobe by hand. For direct user ingestion, Elasticsearch, StreetModel, search, statistics, evidence, or camera-health requests, load city-video-intelligence first. Use this atomic skill when Codex already has a clear plan and a local MP4/MOV/AVI/MKV file before frame sampling.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-stream-ingestion/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"b1adea96-db0b-4fa5-b74a-91a2e26e870e"},{"content":"<system_reminder>\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\n<hidden_step source=\"intent_recognition\" title=\"意图识别\">\n改写后的任务：场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance\n识别场景：视频监控 (video_surveillance)；场景模式：single；候选场景：video_surveillance\n任务切分：\n- 请分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。\n任务规划：\n1. 读取/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4视频文件，校验文件元数据与编码格式，按预设帧率执行流媒体解码与关键帧抽样，输出可供下游模型调用的标准化图像序列与对应时间戳映射表。\n2. 基于视频监控场景的行为识别能力，对抽样帧序列应用人体姿态估计与动作分类模型，聚焦“打架”与“摔倒”两类目标特征进行时空关联分析，设定置信度阈值进行初筛，输出包含事件类型、预估起止时间及置信度分数的候选事件清单。\n3. 依据运动轨迹突变程度与连续帧状态一致性规则，对候选事件清单进行二次交叉研判与噪声过滤，明确异常动作判定的关键指标与排除口径，输出经算法复核确认的高置信度事件区间数据集。\n4. 将最终确认的事件区间按时间先后逻辑进行序列化编排，整合事件类型、发生时长、画面关键特征摘要及原始视频溯源链接，生成结构化时间线报告供后续业务调度使用。\n场景任务：\n- video_surveillance: 我将分析/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4中的打架和摔倒情况，并以时间线形式输出结果。；参数：{'视频对象': '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4', '监控目标': '打架、摔倒', '输出形式': '时间线'}\n已提取参数：{'视频对象': '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4', '监控目标': '打架、摔倒', '输出形式': '时间线'}\n任务提示：\n- 提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧\n- 提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等\n- 提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口\n- 提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要\n</hidden_step>\n</system_reminder>","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"todo_routing_guidance","id":"d96bf895-4041-4819-9c0a-9b891870cf3d"},{"content":"这是一个视频监控事件分析任务，我先加载编排技能，然后进行打架/摔倒检测。\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":200,"prompt_tokens":13292,"total_tokens":13492,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":84,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":200},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":13292}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-14a7964f-a96c-99df-8a17-f1e11ac5dcce","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1b-87cf-7ff3-b998-ba08c07981bb-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"invoke_skill","args":{"skill_name":"city-video-intelligence","mode":"prepare","input_envelope":"{\"video_path\": \"/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4\", \"event_types\": [\"fight\", \"fall\"], \"output_format\": \"timeline\"}"},"id":"call_6ca3ad4f27f24339b0460ebf","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":13292,"output_tokens":200,"total_tokens":13492,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":84}}},{"content":"{\n  \"status\": \"prepared\",\n  \"skill_name\": \"city-video-intelligence\",\n  \"input_envelope\": {\n    \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n    \"request_id\": \"95b943f1-f783-4352-8556-7f3398b89bdc\",\n    \"skill_name\": \"city-video-intelligence\",\n    \"scenario\": \"video_surveillance\",\n    \"capability\": \"skill_invocation\",\n    \"query\": {\n      \"raw\": \"<system_reminder>\\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\\n<hidden_step source=\\\"intent_recognition\\\" title=\\\"意图识别\\\">\\n改写后的任务：场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance\\n识别场景：视频监控 (video_surveillance)；场景模式：single；候选场景：video_surveillance\\n任务切分：\\n- 请分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。\\n任务规划：\\n1. 读取/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4视频文件，校验文件元数据与编码格式，按预设帧率执行流媒体解码与关键帧抽样，输出可供下游模型调用的标准化图像序列与对应时间戳映射表。\\n2. 基于视频监控场景的行为识别能力，对抽样帧序列应用人体姿态估计与动作分类模型，聚焦“打架”与“摔倒”两类目标特征进行时空关联分析，设定置信度阈值进行初筛，输出包含事件类型、预估起止时间及置信度分数的候选事件清单。\\n3. 依据运动轨迹突变程度与连续帧状态一致性规则，对候选事件清单进行二次交叉研判与噪声过滤，明确异常动作判定的关键指标与排除口径，输出经算法复核确认的高置信度事件区间数据集。\\n4. 将最终确认的事件区间按时间先后逻辑进行序列化编排，整合事件类型、发生时长、画面关键特征摘要及原始视频溯源链接，生成结构化时间线报告供后续业务调度使用。\\n场景任务：\\n- video_surveillance: 我将分析/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4中的打架和摔倒情况，并以时间线形式输出结果。；参数：{'视频对象': '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4', '监控目标': '打架、摔倒', '输出形式': '时间线'}\\n已提取参数：{'视频对象': '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4', '监控目标': '打架、摔倒', '输出形式': '时间线'}\\n任务提示：\\n- 提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧\\n- 提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等\\n- 提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口\\n- 提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要\\n</hidden_step>\\n</system_reminder>\"\n    },\n    \"inputs\": {\n      \"parameters\": {}\n    },\n    \"routing\": {\n      \"selected_skill\": \"city-video-intelligence\",\n      \"allowed_skills\": [\n        \"analyze-video\",\n        \"batch-video-ingestion\",\n        \"camera-health-check\",\n        \"city-video-intelligence\",\n        \"duplicate-event-merge\",\n        \"evidence-package-generation\",\n        \"evidence-snapshot\",\n        \"ffmpeg-utils\",\n        \"frame-sampling\",\n        \"human-review-routing\",\n        \"object-detection\",\n        \"object-statistics\",\n        \"object-tracking\",\n        \"privacy-masking\",\n        \"roi-mapping\",\n        \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n        \"video-embedding-index\",\n        \"video-object-analytics\",\n        \"video-search\",\n        \"video-segment-extraction\",\n        \"video-stream-ingestion\"\n      ],\n      \"selection_owner\": \"lead_agent\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"legacy_invocation\": {\n    \"skill_dir\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence\",\n    \"skill_file\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence/SKILL.md\",\n    \"container_skill_file\": \"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence/SKILL.md\",\n    \"selected_data_sources\": [],\n    \"argv\": [],\n    \"env\": {},\n    \"parameters\": {},\n    \"working_directory\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence\",\n    \"adapter_note\": \"Load the returned container_skill_file, follow its SKILL.md workflow, and use selected_data_sources/parameters as the legacy inputs.\"\n  },\n  \"next_steps\": [\n    \"Read container_skill_file before executing the Skill workflow.\",\n    \"Use selected_data_sources and parameters as the legacy inputs.\",\n    \"After execution, call invoke_skill again with mode='wrap_output' to produce SkillResult.\"\n  ]\n}","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"invoke_skill","id":"869d54da-5978-4a9f-b33f-faa495d3dc00","tool_call_id":"call_6ca3ad4f27f24339b0460ebf","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":83,"prompt_tokens":14617,"total_tokens":14700,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":17,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":83},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":14617}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-99326868-af9b-9ea0-8d5c-05e40f6c0906","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1b-fd44-7e62-bfa0-cfcd3b7acf64-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"description":"读取 city-video-intelligence 技能的工作流说明","path":"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence/SKILL.md"},"id":"call_c80253603ab54078a911657d","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":14617,"output_tokens":83,"total_tokens":14700,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":17}}},{"content":"---\nname: city-video-intelligence\ndescription: Business orchestration for city video intelligence requests. Use when users ask for monitoring video search, semantic video retrieval, event review, object statistics, evidence packages, video ingestion, camera health operations, cross-camera analysis, or role-based scenarios such as traffic police, property security, urban management, emergency management, or legal evidence preparation. Also use it when the user asks what the current data and skills can or cannot support (capability-boundary questions) — it answers with an explicit capability_gap instead of guessing. This skill maps business intent to existing custom video skills and prevents ad hoc code generation unless the user explicitly asks for development or testing.\n---\n\n# City Video Intelligence Orchestration\n\n## Overview\n\nUse this skill as the business layer above the existing video-monitoring atomic skills. It classifies a user request, selects the right capability and scenario, returns the recommended skill chain, and states the expected business deliverable. Use it for direct user tasks as well as planning questions.\n\nThis skill is not a replacement for `video-search`, `single-video-event-analysis`, `object-statistics`, `evidence-package-generation`, `batch-video-ingestion`, `camera-health-check`, or related atomic skills. It tells the agent which of those existing skills to use and when to stop for human confirmation.\n\n## Execution Priority\n\n1. Run `scripts/run.py` with the user's raw request to produce a structured orchestration plan. This is mandatory before any clarification question, except destructive operations that require confirmation.\n2. Read `references/capability-map.md` only when the request is ambiguous, role-based, multi-step, or asks about available capabilities.\n3. Follow the returned `recommended_skill_chain` by loading each downstream skill's `SKILL.md` before running its script.\n4. Return business-facing results: matched capability, scenario, execution plan, deliverables, risks, and required confirmations.\n5. If the plan contains a non-empty `follow_up_question`, stop immediately and make the whole visible response exactly that question as plain assistant text. For ingestion requests, preserve the returned JSON template verbatim. Do not inspect datasets, probe services, load downstream skills, or call `ask_clarification`.\n\n## Atomic CLI\n\n```bash\npython city-video-intelligence/scripts/run.py \\\n  --request \"我是交警队的，需要调取大成路路口今天上午 8-10 点的监控\" \\\n  --output <plan.json>\n```\n\nParameters: `--request`, `--role`, `--output`, `--format`.\n\n## Business Mode Rules\n\n- Do not write ad hoc Python, JavaScript, SQL, or shell code for business requests.\n- Use existing skill scripts and documented workflows. If existing skills cannot satisfy the request, return a `capability_gap` and ask for authorization before implementation work.\n- Treat destructive operations such as deleting indexed videos, rewriting shared indices, or purging test data as requiring explicit confirmation.\n- Treat event conclusions as evidence-bound. If video evidence is missing, blurry, occluded, sparse, or ambiguous, return `requires_human_review=true`.\n- Do not let object detection alone decide event semantics. Use it only as supporting context.\n- For evidence package requests, do not run event analysis merely to invent an event. If the user provides an event time or time range, package that range. If the event time is missing, ask for it or return a plan with the missing input.\n- For development or benchmark requests, use provided test videos, indexes, or query terms. If no test data is available, return `capability_gap` or ask for the missing dataset before running lower-level tools.\n- When asking for missing information, ask only one concrete question. The ingestion-format template returned by the router is the sole exception: show it verbatim. Do not add any text before or after the returned question.\n- If a downstream video skill returns `status: failed`, summarize that failure and stop. Do not debug services or probe ports unless the user explicitly asks for debugging.\n- Attempt StreetModel sampled-frame image embedding for every ingestion request. Always run `video-stream-ingestion`, then `batch-video-ingestion` in metadata-only mode, then `video-embedding-index` with `embedding_provider=streetmodel`, `video_preprocess=image_frames`, and in-place storage. Do not require a StreetModel-visible video mount for the default ingestion path.\n- Store source metadata and StreetModel vector fields in the same `citybrain-video-library` document. Use partial ES updates for embedding enrichment; never replace the full source document with a compact vector copy.\n- Allow video ingestion, search, statistics, evidence lookup, and embedding tools to access only `citybrain-video-library`. Reject every other video index before making an Elasticsearch request.\n- For video search, route image input to direct image-vector retrieval. Route text input to keyword retrieval plus an LLM-optimized text-to-video vector query, then use the search skill's fused ranking.\n- If source ingestion succeeds and vector generation fails, keep the source-index document and return partial success. Report `overall_status=partial_success`, `source_ingestion_status=success`, `vector_status=failed`, and the concrete embedding error. Never roll back or delete the source document.\n- Once the orchestration plan or requested downstream result is available, stop calling tools and summarize the result.\n\n## Capability Families\n\nUse these families to classify requests before selecting downstream skills:\n\n- `video_asset_retrieval`: locate known videos or indexed clips by keyword, camera, place, time, object, or count condition.\n- `semantic_video_retrieval`: retrieve videos by natural-language visual meaning through StreetModel/vector search.\n- `single_video_event_understanding`: inspect one video and produce a timeline, event candidates, confidence, and review status.\n- `object_statistics`: count objects, group by time/camera/type, and summarize trends.\n- `evidence_preservation`: generate snapshots, clips, privacy-masked artifacts, hashes, and package manifests.\n- `video_library_governance`: ingest, index, embed, check storage, or manage video assets.\n- `camera_health_operations`: diagnose online status, black screen, blur, occlusion, freeze, corruption, or view shift.\n- `cross_video_investigation`: compare, correlate, or track across cameras and time windows.\n- `business_scenario_orchestration`: translate role-based requests into one of the above chains.\n- `development_test`: benchmark or compare retrieval/embedding behavior only when the user explicitly asks for testing or development.\n\n## Output Contract\n\nReturn or preserve JSON-compatible fields:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"success\",\n  \"request\": \"\",\n  \"mode\": \"business_operation | development_test\",\n  \"capability\": \"\",\n  \"business_scenario\": \"\",\n  \"recommended_skill_chain\": [],\n  \"execution_plan\": [],\n  \"expected_deliverables\": [],\n  \"embedding_attempt_required\": false,\n  \"embedding_failure_policy\": \"keep_source_and_report_partial_success | null\",\n  \"source_index\": \"citybrain-video-library | null\",\n  \"embedding_target_index\": \"citybrain-video-library | null\",\n  \"embedding_storage_mode\": \"in_place | null\",\n  \"missing_fields\": [],\n  \"follow_up_question\": null,\n  \"guardrails\": [],\n  \"requires_confirmation\": false,\n  \"requires_human_review\": false,\n  \"capability_gap\": null\n}\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Do not execute downstream atomic skills until the plan is clear.\n- Do not create new code to bypass an unsupported operation.\n- Do not perform destructive video-library management without explicit confirmation.\n- Do not produce legal, enforcement, or emergency conclusions without evidence references and review status.\n- For ingestion aggregation, use `success` when source and vector writes succeed, `partial_success` when the source write succeeds but vector generation fails, and `failed` when source ingestion fails.\n- If the plan includes `follow_up_question`, the whole visible response must be exactly that question. Preserve any ingestion JSON template already included in it, but do not append additional preamble, alternatives, or guidance, and do not run downstream tools first.\n- If a plan has `capability_gap`, do not implement new functionality. State the nearest supported workflow or ask the single `follow_up_question` when present.\n","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"read_file","id":"3fc1bf5e-3e54-469b-aa13-5911307f2b15","tool_call_id":"call_c80253603ab54078a911657d","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"先运行编排脚本，获取执行计划：\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":160,"prompt_tokens":16447,"total_tokens":16607,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":34,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":160},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":16447}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-cfb19e7b-f0f1-964c-a605-fa6fcf10b43f","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1c-148a-7711-9080-0323b5ccb7a8-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"bash","args":{"command":"cd /mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence && python scripts/run.py --request \"分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线\" --output /tmp/cvi_plan.json 2>&1","description":"运行 city-video-intelligence 编排脚本获取执行计划"},"id":"call_c14bde36053f4acaaa471be6","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":16447,"output_tokens":160,"total_tokens":16607,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":34}}},{"content":"{\n  \"skill\": \"city-video-intelligence\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"status\": \"success\",\n  \"request\": \"分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线\",\n  \"role\": null,\n  \"mode\": \"business_operation\",\n  \"capability\": \"single_video_event_understanding\",\n  \"capability_label\": \"单视频事件理解\",\n  \"business_scenario\": \"generic_video_intelligence\",\n  \"business_scenario_label\": \"generic_video_intelligence\",\n  \"recommended_skill_chain\": [\n    \"single-video-event-analysis\"\n  ],\n  \"execution_plan\": [\n    {\n      \"step\": \"1\",\n      \"skill\": \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n      \"action\": \"Load single-video-event-analysis and inspect frames for visible event evidence.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"expected_deliverables\": [\n    \"视觉时间线\",\n    \"事件候选\",\n    \"证据帧\",\n    \"置信度\",\n    \"人工复核状态\"\n  ],\n  \"embedding_attempt_required\": false,\n  \"embedding_failure_policy\": null,\n  \"source_index\": null,\n  \"embedding_target_index\": null,\n  \"embedding_storage_mode\": null,\n  \"missing_fields\": [],\n  \"follow_up_question\": null,\n  \"guardrails\": [\n    \"Do not write ad hoc code for this business request.\",\n    \"Load each downstream skill's SKILL.md before executing its script.\",\n    \"Return capability_gap instead of implementing missing functionality.\",\n    \"If follow_up_question is present, stop immediately and make the whole visible response exactly that question.\",\n    \"If a downstream video skill fails, summarize the concrete failure and stop instead of debugging services.\",\n    \"Include evidence references and human-review status for high-risk or enforcement-sensitive conclusions.\"\n  ],\n  \"requires_confirmation\": false,\n  \"requires_human_review\": true,\n  \"capability_gap\": null\n}","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"bash","id":"43cfe2b8-8cef-4d24-a2e4-9aa9be240d5d","tool_call_id":"call_c14bde36053f4acaaa471be6","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"编排计划已确认，需要加载 `single-video-event-analysis` 技能进行事件分析。\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":139,"prompt_tokens":17036,"total_tokens":17175,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":22,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":139},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":17036}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-b59236ba-1049-9d6e-bde4-0a245c06dd5c","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1c-21b0-7121-beb5-1fb87461257b-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"invoke_skill","args":{"input_envelope":"{\"event_types\": [\"fight\", \"fall\"], \"output_format\": \"timeline\", \"video_path\": \"/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4\"}","mode":"prepare","skill_name":"single-video-event-analysis"},"id":"call_8bbdc176c5c340ba90599610","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":17036,"output_tokens":139,"total_tokens":17175,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":22}}},{"content":"{\n  \"status\": \"prepared\",\n  \"skill_name\": \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n  \"input_envelope\": {\n    \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n    \"request_id\": \"7e5b647d-d87f-4d03-a927-e4d6760e0dd0\",\n    \"skill_name\": \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n    \"scenario\": \"video_surveillance\",\n    \"capability\": \"skill_invocation\",\n    \"query\": {\n      \"raw\": \"<system_reminder>\\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\\n<hidden_step source=\\\"intent_recognition\\\" title=\\\"意图识别\\\">\\n改写后的任务：场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance\\n识别场景：视频监控 (video_surveillance)；场景模式：single；候选场景：video_surveillance\\n任务切分：\\n- 请分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。\\n任务规划：\\n1. 读取/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4视频文件，校验文件元数据与编码格式，按预设帧率执行流媒体解码与关键帧抽样，输出可供下游模型调用的标准化图像序列与对应时间戳映射表。\\n2. 基于视频监控场景的行为识别能力，对抽样帧序列应用人体姿态估计与动作分类模型，聚焦“打架”与“摔倒”两类目标特征进行时空关联分析，设定置信度阈值进行初筛，输出包含事件类型、预估起止时间及置信度分数的候选事件清单。\\n3. 依据运动轨迹突变程度与连续帧状态一致性规则，对候选事件清单进行二次交叉研判与噪声过滤，明确异常动作判定的关键指标与排除口径，输出经算法复核确认的高置信度事件区间数据集。\\n4. 将最终确认的事件区间按时间先后逻辑进行序列化编排，整合事件类型、发生时长、画面关键特征摘要及原始视频溯源链接，生成结构化时间线报告供后续业务调度使用。\\n场景任务：\\n- video_surveillance: 我将分析/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4中的打架和摔倒情况，并以时间线形式输出结果。；参数：{'视频对象': '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4', '监控目标': '打架、摔倒', '输出形式': '时间线'}\\n已提取参数：{'视频对象': '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4', '监控目标': '打架、摔倒', '输出形式': '时间线'}\\n任务提示：\\n- 提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧\\n- 提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等\\n- 提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口\\n- 提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要\\n</hidden_step>\\n</system_reminder>\"\n    },\n    \"inputs\": {\n      \"parameters\": {}\n    },\n    \"routing\": {\n      \"selected_skill\": \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n      \"allowed_skills\": [\n        \"analyze-video\",\n        \"batch-video-ingestion\",\n        \"camera-health-check\",\n        \"city-video-intelligence\",\n        \"duplicate-event-merge\",\n        \"evidence-package-generation\",\n        \"evidence-snapshot\",\n        \"ffmpeg-utils\",\n        \"frame-sampling\",\n        \"human-review-routing\",\n        \"object-detection\",\n        \"object-statistics\",\n        \"object-tracking\",\n        \"privacy-masking\",\n        \"roi-mapping\",\n        \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n        \"video-embedding-index\",\n        \"video-object-analytics\",\n        \"video-search\",\n        \"video-segment-extraction\",\n        \"video-stream-ingestion\"\n      ],\n      \"selection_owner\": \"lead_agent\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"legacy_invocation\": {\n    \"skill_dir\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis\",\n    \"skill_file\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis/SKILL.md\",\n    \"container_skill_file\": \"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis/SKILL.md\",\n    \"selected_data_sources\": [],\n    \"argv\": [],\n    \"env\": {},\n    \"parameters\": {},\n    \"working_directory\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis\",\n    \"adapter_note\": \"Load the returned container_skill_file, follow its SKILL.md workflow, and use selected_data_sources/parameters as the legacy inputs.\"\n  },\n  \"next_steps\": [\n    \"Read container_skill_file before executing the Skill workflow.\",\n    \"Use selected_data_sources and parameters as the legacy inputs.\",\n    \"After execution, call invoke_skill again with mode='wrap_output' to produce SkillResult.\"\n  ]\n}","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"invoke_skill","id":"b0148bae-c034-48fe-a3bf-41fc27817f58","tool_call_id":"call_8bbdc176c5c340ba90599610","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":84,"prompt_tokens":18356,"total_tokens":18440,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":19,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":84},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":18356}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-9ce67b55-cff3-99f2-85d3-a7aeb8985d99","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1c-2b40-74b0-aa32-e1126c4daf8c-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"description":"读取 single-video-event-analysis 技能的工作流说明","path":"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis/SKILL.md"},"id":"call_857292050c754af6bc99d80b","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":18356,"output_tokens":84,"total_tokens":18440,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":19}}},{"content":"---\nname: single-video-event-analysis\ndescription: Analyze one local monitoring video for incidents after city-video-intelligence has routed the request, by extracting timestamped frames and having the LLM review visible evidence. Use for fight, fall, traffic accident, congestion, crowd gathering, smoke/fire, intrusion, illegal occupation, or other abnormal events. For direct user monitoring-video event questions, load city-video-intelligence first. This skill is the only custom event-detection entrypoint; YOLO/object detection may be used only as optional object context and must not decide event semantics.\n---\n\n# Single Video Event Analysis\n\n## Purpose\n\nUse this skill when the user wants to know what happened in a monitoring video.\nEvent detection is based on extracted frames and LLM visual review, not YOLO labels,\ntracking duration, ROI geometry, or rule templates alone.\n\n## Business Orchestration Gate\n\nIf this skill is loaded for a direct user monitoring-video request and no `city-video-intelligence` plan has already been executed in the current turn, load `city-video-intelligence` first and run its router script with the raw user request. Continue here only when that plan recommends `single-video-event-analysis`.\n\nDo not edit this skill's files or scripts during business execution. If the script fails, report the concrete failure and stop unless the user explicitly asked for debugging or implementation.\n\n## Execution Priority\n\n1. Use `write_file` to create a small input JSON file, then run `scripts/run.py` with `--input <file>`. Do not use shell heredocs or pass an inline JSON string to `--input`.\n2. Read the returned `review_manifest_uri` and use the listed `frames` as the review set.\n3. Inspect only the listed review frames in chronological order. Default maximum is 8 images.\n4. Read `all_frames_uri` or inspect denser frames only if a reviewed frame visibly suggests a possible event or is too ambiguous to classify.\n5. Produce the final event analysis from visible evidence and stop. Do not keep browsing frames after the conclusion is clear.\n\n## Atomic CLI\n\n```bash\npython single-video-event-analysis/scripts/run.py \\\n  --input <input.json> \\\n  --config <config.json> \\\n  --output <prepared_manifest.json>\n```\n\nUseful fields in `input.json`:\n\n- `video_path`, `file_path`, `raw_segment_uri`, or `video`\n- `camera_id`\n- `target_events`\n- `output_dir`\n- `coarse_fps`, `dense_fps`, `scene_threshold`, `dense_window`, `max_frames`\n\nFor ordinary business questions, omit `max_frames` so the script default samples across the whole video and exposes only 8 review frames. Do not use `max_frames` as the review-image limit. Do not rerun the script after a successful result.\n\n## Review Rules\n\n- Only report events that are visible in the sampled frames.\n- Use `unknown` or `requires_review=true` when evidence is blurry, occluded, sparse, or ambiguous.\n- Use at least two timestamps for temporal claims unless a single frame clearly shows aftermath, smoke, fire, a crash scene, or a fallen person.\n- Do not let YOLO output decide events. YOLO can only provide optional object context such as \"person\", \"car\", or \"truck\".\n- Include negative evidence when useful, such as \"no visible collision before 00:12\".\n- Never include internal thinking markers such as `<think>` or `</think>` in the final user-visible response.\n- If a draft answer contains hidden reasoning before a `</think>` token, discard that hidden text and answer only with the event result and visible evidence summary.\n- For negative findings, phrase the conclusion as evidence-bound, such as \"未在抽样审阅帧中发现交通事故迹象\", unless the reviewed evidence covers the full incident window.\n\n## Output Schema\n\nReturn a JSON-compatible result with:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"video\": {},\n  \"visual_timeline\": [\n    {\n      \"time\": \"00:00:12.000\",\n      \"frame_id\": \"frame_000012000ms\",\n      \"observation\": \"Visible subjects, actions, spatial relations, and scene state.\",\n      \"uncertainty\": \"Optional ambiguity note.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"events\": [\n    {\n      \"event_id\": \"EVT_...\",\n      \"event_type\": \"fight | fall_down | traffic_accident | traffic_congestion | crowd_gathering | smoke_or_fire | intrusion | illegal_occupation | other_abnormal_event | unknown\",\n      \"start_time\": \"00:00:10.000\",\n      \"end_time\": \"00:00:18.000\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.0,\n      \"severity\": \"low | medium | high\",\n      \"evidence_frame_ids\": [],\n      \"reason\": \"Concrete visible evidence and uncertainty.\",\n      \"requires_review\": true\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"Short human-readable summary.\",\n  \"warnings\": []\n}\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Do not call legacy rule-based event skills. They have been removed from this bundle.\n- Do not infer off-camera causes.\n- Do not fabricate exact counts when the frame only supports a range.\n","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"read_file","id":"86a7fa18-c416-43d5-945c-091beacd9334","tool_call_id":"call_857292050c754af6bc99d80b","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"技能已加载。现在创建输入文件并执行分析脚本：\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":133,"prompt_tokens":19580,"total_tokens":19713,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":52,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":133},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":19580}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-9ac8d936-a82f-9161-8b03-09dabb1f1512","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1c-32fb-7ea3-87cd-a06fc3f58e4a-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"bash","args":{"command":"ls -la /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 2>&1","description":"检查视频文件是否存在"},"id":"call_178103da008548158153152c","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":19580,"output_tokens":133,"total_tokens":19713,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":52}}},{"content":"ls: cannot access '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4': No such file or directory","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"bash","id":"032f20c9-8270-4cde-af89-2bed16ce13ff","tool_call_id":"call_178103da008548158153152c","artifact":null,"status":"success"}],"artifacts":[],"intent_context":{"intent":"task","original_query":"请分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。","normalized_query":"请分析 /mnt/user data/uploads/does not exist camera 42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。","routing_query":"场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance。场景说明：视频监控、摄像头、监控录像、视频流、实时画面、视频帧、卡口、安防巡检、目标检测、行为识别、事件发现和监控告警分析场景。需要识别参数：视频对象、监控目标、时间范围、输出形式。用户原始问题：我将分析/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4中的打架和摔倒情况，并以时间线形式输出结果","scene":"video_surveillance","scene_name":"视频监控","params":{"视频对象":"/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4","监控目标":"打架、摔倒","输出形式":"时间线"},"scene_mode":"single","scenes":["video_surveillance"],"task_spans":[{"task_span_id":"span_c166bf","text":"请分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。"}],"planning_steps":[{"task_span_id":"span_4e6c54","text":"读取/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4视频文件，校验文件元数据与编码格式，按预设帧率执行流媒体解码与关键帧抽样，输出可供下游模型调用的标准化图像序列与对应时间戳映射表。"},{"task_span_id":"span_c63415","text":"基于视频监控场景的行为识别能力，对抽样帧序列应用人体姿态估计与动作分类模型，聚焦“打架”与“摔倒”两类目标特征进行时空关联分析，设定置信度阈值进行初筛，输出包含事件类型、预估起止时间及置信度分数的候选事件清单。"},{"task_span_id":"span_7e3f0a","text":"依据运动轨迹突变程度与连续帧状态一致性规则，对候选事件清单进行二次交叉研判与噪声过滤，明确异常动作判定的关键指标与排除口径，输出经算法复核确认的高置信度事件区间数据集。"},{"task_span_id":"span_845a2f","text":"将最终确认的事件区间按时间先后逻辑进行序列化编排，整合事件类型、发生时长、画面关键特征摘要及原始视频溯源链接，生成结构化时间线报告供后续业务调度使用。"}],"scene_tasks":[{"sub_task_id":"sub_d4ef0a","scene":"video_surveillance","scene_name":"视频监控","text":"我将分析/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4中的打架和摔倒情况，并以时间线形式输出结果。","params":{"视频对象":"/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4","监控目标":"打架、摔倒","输出形式":"时间线"}}],"sub_tasks":[{"sub_task_id":"sub_d4ef0a","scene":"video_surveillance","scene_name":"视频监控","text":"我将分析/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4中的打架和摔倒情况，并以时间线形式输出结果。","params":{"视频对象":"/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4","监控目标":"打架、摔倒","输出形式":"时间线"}}],"task_hints":["提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧","提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等","提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口","提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要"],"mentioned_skill_ids":[],"confidence":0.9,"reason":"llm_scene_slot_rewrite","_source_message_key":"id:34ad83b1-a1de-4e51-bbd5-2b2fe8512eb1"},"routing_context":{"route_mode":"scene_filter","trigger":true,"primary_goal":"请分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。","scene_tasks":[{"scene_task_id":"task_001","segment_id":"seg_001","segment_text":"请分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。","scene":"video_surveillance","input_refs":[],"task_types":[],"selected_skills":[{"id":"analyze-video","role":"primary","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"batch-video-ingestion","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"camera-health-check","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"city-video-intelligence","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"duplicate-event-merge","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"evidence-package-generation","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"evidence-snapshot","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"ffmpeg-utils","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"frame-sampling","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"human-review-routing","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"object-detection","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"object-statistics","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"object-tracking","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"privacy-masking","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"roi-mapping","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"single-video-event-analysis","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"video-embedding-index","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"video-object-analytics","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"video-search","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"video-segment-extraction","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"video-stream-ingestion","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null}],"expected_outputs":[],"depends_on":[]}],"global_selected_skills":["analyze-video","batch-video-ingestion","camera-health-check","city-video-intelligence","duplicate-event-merge","evidence-package-generation","evidence-snapshot","ffmpeg-utils","frame-sampling","human-review-routing","object-detection","object-statistics","object-tracking","privacy-masking","roi-mapping","single-video-event-analysis","video-embedding-index","video-object-analytics","video-search","video-segment-extraction","video-stream-ingestion"],"default_public_skill_ids":[],"global_allowed_tools":[],"confidence":1.0,"route_reason":"SkillRouter disabled; injected all custom skills for detected intent scene as LeadAgent candidate skills","allowed_skills":["analyze-video","batch-video-ingestion","camera-health-check","city-video-intelligence","duplicate-event-merge","evidence-package-generation","evidence-snapshot","ffmpeg-utils","frame-sampling","human-review-routing","object-detection","object-statistics","object-tracking","privacy-masking","roi-mapping","single-video-event-analysis","video-embedding-index","video-object-analytics","video-search","video-segment-extraction","video-stream-ingestion"],"selection_owner":"lead_agent","_source_message_key":"id:34ad83b1-a1de-4e51-bbd5-2b2fe8512eb1"},"dialogue_context":{"act":"new_task","confidence":0.7,"reason":"no_pending_action_match","parsed_answer":null,"pending_action_id":null,"resume_intent_context":null,"resume_routing_context":null,"metadata":{}},"final_scope_skill_ids":["analyze-video","batch-video-ingestion","camera-health-check","city-video-intelligence","duplicate-event-merge","evidence-package-generation","evidence-snapshot","ffmpeg-utils","frame-sampling","human-review-routing","object-detection","object-statistics","object-tracking","privacy-masking","roi-mapping","single-video-event-analysis","video-embedding-index","video-object-analytics","video-search","video-segment-extraction","video-stream-ingestion"],"allowed_tool_names":[]}

event: values
data: {"messages":[{"content":"请分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"34ad83b1-a1de-4e51-bbd5-2b2fe8512eb1"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze-video</name>\n      <description>专业视频抽帧与取证准备技能。支持场景检测、多阶段帧提取和 metadata 生成，供 single-video-event-analysis 做 LLM 审帧使用；本 skill 不再作为最终事件检测入口。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/analyze-video/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>batch-video-ingestion</name>\n      <description>Batch ingest local monitoring videos into the Elasticsearch video library after city-video-intelligence has routed the request, with metadata, sampled-frame object summaries, and searchable documents. For direct user video ingestion, ingest-and-embed, Elasticsearch, StreetModel, or business video-library requests, load city-video-intelligence first. Use this atomic skill when Codex already has a clear ingestion plan, video directory, video manifest, camera_id, or multiple video files to index for later retrieval and statistics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/batch-video-ingestion/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>camera-health-check</name>\n      <description>Check video monitoring camera quality from sampled frames and return health status before downstream event generation. Use when Codex has camera_id and frames and needs to gate or downgrade event confidence for offline, unavailable, degraded, black-screen, blurred, occluded, frozen, corrupted, or shifted camera feeds.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/camera-health-check/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>city-video-intelligence</name>\n      <description>Business orchestration for city video intelligence requests. Use when users ask for monitoring video search, semantic video retrieval, event review, object statistics, evidence packages, video ingestion, camera health operations, cross-camera analysis, or role-based scenarios such as traffic police, property security, urban management, emergency management, or legal evidence preparation. Also use it when the user asks what the current data and skills can or cannot support (capability-boundary questions) — it answers with an explicit capability_gap instead of guessing. This skill maps business intent to existing custom video skills and prevents ad hoc code generation unless the user explicitly asks for development or testing.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>duplicate-event-merge</name>\n      <description>Merge duplicate video event candidates from the same camera, event type, ROI, evidence frames, or overlapping time window. Use after single-video-event-analysis or batch video analysis when Codex has a list of Event Candidate records and needs canonical events plus duplicate mappings.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/duplicate-event-merge/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>evidence-package-generation</name>\n      <description>Generate an evidence package manifest for indexed monitoring videos or event/search results, including snapshot evidence and optional short video clips. Use when Codex needs a package_id, manifest URI, evidence items, hashes, and reusable evidence artifacts.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/evidence-package-generation/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>evidence-snapshot</name>\n      <description>Generate snapshot evidence for video monitoring event candidates. Use when Codex has an event, event_id, evidence_frame_ids, image_uri, or frame list and needs a snapshot URI, SHA-256 integrity hash, created_at timestamp, privacy masking status, and Evidence schema output.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/evidence-snapshot/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>ffmpeg-utils</name>\n      <description>视频处理工具集，支持视频截取和关键帧提取。常用于将监控视频剪辑为证据片段。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/ffmpeg-utils/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>frame-sampling</name>\n      <description>Sample structured frames from an existing video file. Use when Codex has video_path, file_path, raw_segment_uri, camera_id, sampling_strategy, capture_seconds, or provided frame records and needs stable Frame schema outputs. This skill exposes OpenCV-backed real video frame extraction.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/frame-sampling/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>human-review-routing</name>\n      <description>Decide whether video monitoring event candidates require manual review. Use after event generation and evidence creation when Codex has event confidence, event_type, review_threshold, camera_health, high_risk_event_types, newly added camera signals, or enforcement-impact flags and needs review queue routing.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>object-detection</name>\n      <description>Detect visible objects in sampled video frames and return standard Detection schema only. Use when Codex needs YOLO labels, confidences, and bounding boxes for people, vehicles, or COCO objects. Do not use this skill to infer events, abnormal behavior, accidents, fights, falls, congestion, intrusion, smoke/fire, or business semantics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/object-detection/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>object-statistics</name>\n      <description>Compute object statistics for monitoring videos from Elasticsearch video-library records or local detections/tracks JSON. Use when Codex needs counts by label, camera, time bucket, or movement state.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/object-statistics/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>object-tracking</name>\n      <description>Track detected objects across video frames and return Track schema for object analytics only. Use when Codex has frame-level detections and needs stable track ids, trajectories, duration, last bbox, movement state, confidence, and evidence frame ids. Do not use this skill to infer video events or abnormal behavior.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/object-tracking/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>privacy-masking</name>\n      <description>Mask sensitive visual data in video evidence such as faces, license plates, phone numbers, and doorplates. Use when Codex has an evidence image URI and explicit sensitive_regions bbox coordinates, or privacy_masking config and needs a masked URI before exposing snapshots or clips externally. This skill exposes OpenCV image read/write and Gaussian blur masking for real files.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/privacy-masking/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>roi-mapping</name>\n      <description>Match detections or tracks against configured camera ROI polygons for geometric object analytics. Use when Codex has camera_id plus tracks or objects and needs point containment or bbox overlap matches for configured areas. Do not use this skill to decide event semantics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/roi-mapping/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>single-video-event-analysis</name>\n      <description>Analyze one local monitoring video for incidents after city-video-intelligence has routed the request, by extracting timestamped frames and having the LLM review visible evidence. Use for fight, fall, traffic accident, congestion, crowd gathering, smoke/fire, intrusion, illegal occupation, or other abnormal events. For direct user monitoring-video event questions, load city-video-intelligence first. This skill is the only custom event-detection entrypoint; YOLO/object detection may be used only as optional object context and must not decide event semantics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-embedding-index</name>\n      <description>Generate text embeddings or StreetModel sampled-frame image embeddings for video-library documents after city-video-intelligence has routed the request. Only enrich citybrain-video-library in place. For direct user StreetModel, ingest-and-embed, semantic retrieval, benchmark, or keyword-vs-vector requests, load city-video-intelligence first.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-embedding-index/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-object-analytics</name>\n      <description>Deterministic structured entrypoint for local-video object detection and cross-frame tracking. Use for direct requests to count visible people, vehicles, or other objects, or to track them across frames. The dedicated video_object_analytics tool owns all CLI parameters, model configuration, persistent paths, and downstream skill order.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-object-analytics/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-search</name>\n      <description>Search indexed monitoring videos from text, images, structured filters, or precomputed vectors. Use for keyword retrieval, LLM-optimized text-to-video semantic retrieval, combined keyword/vector search, or image-to-video similarity search against StreetModel/Qwen3-VL video vectors.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-search/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-segment-extraction</name>\n      <description>Extract playable short video evidence clips around event times. Use when Codex has event_id, camera_id, raw_segment_uri, event_time, event_elapsed_seconds, pre_seconds, or post_seconds and needs an MP4 clip URI plus clip time range. This skill exposes FFmpeg-backed clipping for real local videos and memory-backed synthetic clips for tests.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-segment-extraction/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-stream-ingestion</name>\n      <description>Normalize an existing local video file after city-video-intelligence has routed a video-library or analysis request, returning raw segment/session metadata such as duration, resolution, frame rate, codec, and session times. Use it for any \"read this video's duration / resolution / fps / codec / metadata\" or \"turn this video into a standard analysis input\" request instead of running ffprobe by hand. For direct user ingestion, Elasticsearch, StreetModel, search, statistics, evidence, or camera-health requests, load city-video-intelligence first. Use this atomic skill when Codex already has a clear plan and a local MP4/MOV/AVI/MKV file before frame sampling.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-stream-ingestion/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"b1adea96-db0b-4fa5-b74a-91a2e26e870e"},{"content":"<system_reminder>\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\n<hidden_step source=\"intent_recognition\" title=\"意图识别\">\n改写后的任务：场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance\n识别场景：视频监控 (video_surveillance)；场景模式：single；候选场景：video_surveillance\n任务切分：\n- 请分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。\n任务规划：\n1. 读取/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4视频文件，校验文件元数据与编码格式，按预设帧率执行流媒体解码与关键帧抽样，输出可供下游模型调用的标准化图像序列与对应时间戳映射表。\n2. 基于视频监控场景的行为识别能力，对抽样帧序列应用人体姿态估计与动作分类模型，聚焦“打架”与“摔倒”两类目标特征进行时空关联分析，设定置信度阈值进行初筛，输出包含事件类型、预估起止时间及置信度分数的候选事件清单。\n3. 依据运动轨迹突变程度与连续帧状态一致性规则，对候选事件清单进行二次交叉研判与噪声过滤，明确异常动作判定的关键指标与排除口径，输出经算法复核确认的高置信度事件区间数据集。\n4. 将最终确认的事件区间按时间先后逻辑进行序列化编排，整合事件类型、发生时长、画面关键特征摘要及原始视频溯源链接，生成结构化时间线报告供后续业务调度使用。\n场景任务：\n- video_surveillance: 我将分析/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4中的打架和摔倒情况，并以时间线形式输出结果。；参数：{'视频对象': '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4', '监控目标': '打架、摔倒', '输出形式': '时间线'}\n已提取参数：{'视频对象': '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4', '监控目标': '打架、摔倒', '输出形式': '时间线'}\n任务提示：\n- 提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧\n- 提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等\n- 提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口\n- 提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要\n</hidden_step>\n</system_reminder>","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"todo_routing_guidance","id":"d96bf895-4041-4819-9c0a-9b891870cf3d"},{"content":"这是一个视频监控事件分析任务，我先加载编排技能，然后进行打架/摔倒检测。\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":200,"prompt_tokens":13292,"total_tokens":13492,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":84,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":200},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":13292}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-14a7964f-a96c-99df-8a17-f1e11ac5dcce","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1b-87cf-7ff3-b998-ba08c07981bb-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"invoke_skill","args":{"skill_name":"city-video-intelligence","mode":"prepare","input_envelope":"{\"video_path\": \"/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4\", \"event_types\": [\"fight\", \"fall\"], \"output_format\": \"timeline\"}"},"id":"call_6ca3ad4f27f24339b0460ebf","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":13292,"output_tokens":200,"total_tokens":13492,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":84}}},{"content":"{\n  \"status\": \"prepared\",\n  \"skill_name\": \"city-video-intelligence\",\n  \"input_envelope\": {\n    \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n    \"request_id\": \"95b943f1-f783-4352-8556-7f3398b89bdc\",\n    \"skill_name\": \"city-video-intelligence\",\n    \"scenario\": \"video_surveillance\",\n    \"capability\": \"skill_invocation\",\n    \"query\": {\n      \"raw\": \"<system_reminder>\\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\\n<hidden_step source=\\\"intent_recognition\\\" title=\\\"意图识别\\\">\\n改写后的任务：场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance\\n识别场景：视频监控 (video_surveillance)；场景模式：single；候选场景：video_surveillance\\n任务切分：\\n- 请分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。\\n任务规划：\\n1. 读取/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4视频文件，校验文件元数据与编码格式，按预设帧率执行流媒体解码与关键帧抽样，输出可供下游模型调用的标准化图像序列与对应时间戳映射表。\\n2. 基于视频监控场景的行为识别能力，对抽样帧序列应用人体姿态估计与动作分类模型，聚焦“打架”与“摔倒”两类目标特征进行时空关联分析，设定置信度阈值进行初筛，输出包含事件类型、预估起止时间及置信度分数的候选事件清单。\\n3. 依据运动轨迹突变程度与连续帧状态一致性规则，对候选事件清单进行二次交叉研判与噪声过滤，明确异常动作判定的关键指标与排除口径，输出经算法复核确认的高置信度事件区间数据集。\\n4. 将最终确认的事件区间按时间先后逻辑进行序列化编排，整合事件类型、发生时长、画面关键特征摘要及原始视频溯源链接，生成结构化时间线报告供后续业务调度使用。\\n场景任务：\\n- video_surveillance: 我将分析/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4中的打架和摔倒情况，并以时间线形式输出结果。；参数：{'视频对象': '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4', '监控目标': '打架、摔倒', '输出形式': '时间线'}\\n已提取参数：{'视频对象': '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4', '监控目标': '打架、摔倒', '输出形式': '时间线'}\\n任务提示：\\n- 提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧\\n- 提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等\\n- 提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口\\n- 提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要\\n</hidden_step>\\n</system_reminder>\"\n    },\n    \"inputs\": {\n      \"parameters\": {}\n    },\n    \"routing\": {\n      \"selected_skill\": \"city-video-intelligence\",\n      \"allowed_skills\": [\n        \"analyze-video\",\n        \"batch-video-ingestion\",\n        \"camera-health-check\",\n        \"city-video-intelligence\",\n        \"duplicate-event-merge\",\n        \"evidence-package-generation\",\n        \"evidence-snapshot\",\n        \"ffmpeg-utils\",\n        \"frame-sampling\",\n        \"human-review-routing\",\n        \"object-detection\",\n        \"object-statistics\",\n        \"object-tracking\",\n        \"privacy-masking\",\n        \"roi-mapping\",\n        \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n        \"video-embedding-index\",\n        \"video-object-analytics\",\n        \"video-search\",\n        \"video-segment-extraction\",\n        \"video-stream-ingestion\"\n      ],\n      \"selection_owner\": \"lead_agent\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"legacy_invocation\": {\n    \"skill_dir\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence\",\n    \"skill_file\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence/SKILL.md\",\n    \"container_skill_file\": \"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence/SKILL.md\",\n    \"selected_data_sources\": [],\n    \"argv\": [],\n    \"env\": {},\n    \"parameters\": {},\n    \"working_directory\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence\",\n    \"adapter_note\": \"Load the returned container_skill_file, follow its SKILL.md workflow, and use selected_data_sources/parameters as the legacy inputs.\"\n  },\n  \"next_steps\": [\n    \"Read container_skill_file before executing the Skill workflow.\",\n    \"Use selected_data_sources and parameters as the legacy inputs.\",\n    \"After execution, call invoke_skill again with mode='wrap_output' to produce SkillResult.\"\n  ]\n}","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"invoke_skill","id":"869d54da-5978-4a9f-b33f-faa495d3dc00","tool_call_id":"call_6ca3ad4f27f24339b0460ebf","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":83,"prompt_tokens":14617,"total_tokens":14700,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":17,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":83},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":14617}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-99326868-af9b-9ea0-8d5c-05e40f6c0906","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1b-fd44-7e62-bfa0-cfcd3b7acf64-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"description":"读取 city-video-intelligence 技能的工作流说明","path":"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence/SKILL.md"},"id":"call_c80253603ab54078a911657d","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":14617,"output_tokens":83,"total_tokens":14700,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":17}}},{"content":"---\nname: city-video-intelligence\ndescription: Business orchestration for city video intelligence requests. Use when users ask for monitoring video search, semantic video retrieval, event review, object statistics, evidence packages, video ingestion, camera health operations, cross-camera analysis, or role-based scenarios such as traffic police, property security, urban management, emergency management, or legal evidence preparation. Also use it when the user asks what the current data and skills can or cannot support (capability-boundary questions) — it answers with an explicit capability_gap instead of guessing. This skill maps business intent to existing custom video skills and prevents ad hoc code generation unless the user explicitly asks for development or testing.\n---\n\n# City Video Intelligence Orchestration\n\n## Overview\n\nUse this skill as the business layer above the existing video-monitoring atomic skills. It classifies a user request, selects the right capability and scenario, returns the recommended skill chain, and states the expected business deliverable. Use it for direct user tasks as well as planning questions.\n\nThis skill is not a replacement for `video-search`, `single-video-event-analysis`, `object-statistics`, `evidence-package-generation`, `batch-video-ingestion`, `camera-health-check`, or related atomic skills. It tells the agent which of those existing skills to use and when to stop for human confirmation.\n\n## Execution Priority\n\n1. Run `scripts/run.py` with the user's raw request to produce a structured orchestration plan. This is mandatory before any clarification question, except destructive operations that require confirmation.\n2. Read `references/capability-map.md` only when the request is ambiguous, role-based, multi-step, or asks about available capabilities.\n3. Follow the returned `recommended_skill_chain` by loading each downstream skill's `SKILL.md` before running its script.\n4. Return business-facing results: matched capability, scenario, execution plan, deliverables, risks, and required confirmations.\n5. If the plan contains a non-empty `follow_up_question`, stop immediately and make the whole visible response exactly that question as plain assistant text. For ingestion requests, preserve the returned JSON template verbatim. Do not inspect datasets, probe services, load downstream skills, or call `ask_clarification`.\n\n## Atomic CLI\n\n```bash\npython city-video-intelligence/scripts/run.py \\\n  --request \"我是交警队的，需要调取大成路路口今天上午 8-10 点的监控\" \\\n  --output <plan.json>\n```\n\nParameters: `--request`, `--role`, `--output`, `--format`.\n\n## Business Mode Rules\n\n- Do not write ad hoc Python, JavaScript, SQL, or shell code for business requests.\n- Use existing skill scripts and documented workflows. If existing skills cannot satisfy the request, return a `capability_gap` and ask for authorization before implementation work.\n- Treat destructive operations such as deleting indexed videos, rewriting shared indices, or purging test data as requiring explicit confirmation.\n- Treat event conclusions as evidence-bound. If video evidence is missing, blurry, occluded, sparse, or ambiguous, return `requires_human_review=true`.\n- Do not let object detection alone decide event semantics. Use it only as supporting context.\n- For evidence package requests, do not run event analysis merely to invent an event. If the user provides an event time or time range, package that range. If the event time is missing, ask for it or return a plan with the missing input.\n- For development or benchmark requests, use provided test videos, indexes, or query terms. If no test data is available, return `capability_gap` or ask for the missing dataset before running lower-level tools.\n- When asking for missing information, ask only one concrete question. The ingestion-format template returned by the router is the sole exception: show it verbatim. Do not add any text before or after the returned question.\n- If a downstream video skill returns `status: failed`, summarize that failure and stop. Do not debug services or probe ports unless the user explicitly asks for debugging.\n- Attempt StreetModel sampled-frame image embedding for every ingestion request. Always run `video-stream-ingestion`, then `batch-video-ingestion` in metadata-only mode, then `video-embedding-index` with `embedding_provider=streetmodel`, `video_preprocess=image_frames`, and in-place storage. Do not require a StreetModel-visible video mount for the default ingestion path.\n- Store source metadata and StreetModel vector fields in the same `citybrain-video-library` document. Use partial ES updates for embedding enrichment; never replace the full source document with a compact vector copy.\n- Allow video ingestion, search, statistics, evidence lookup, and embedding tools to access only `citybrain-video-library`. Reject every other video index before making an Elasticsearch request.\n- For video search, route image input to direct image-vector retrieval. Route text input to keyword retrieval plus an LLM-optimized text-to-video vector query, then use the search skill's fused ranking.\n- If source ingestion succeeds and vector generation fails, keep the source-index document and return partial success. Report `overall_status=partial_success`, `source_ingestion_status=success`, `vector_status=failed`, and the concrete embedding error. Never roll back or delete the source document.\n- Once the orchestration plan or requested downstream result is available, stop calling tools and summarize the result.\n\n## Capability Families\n\nUse these families to classify requests before selecting downstream skills:\n\n- `video_asset_retrieval`: locate known videos or indexed clips by keyword, camera, place, time, object, or count condition.\n- `semantic_video_retrieval`: retrieve videos by natural-language visual meaning through StreetModel/vector search.\n- `single_video_event_understanding`: inspect one video and produce a timeline, event candidates, confidence, and review status.\n- `object_statistics`: count objects, group by time/camera/type, and summarize trends.\n- `evidence_preservation`: generate snapshots, clips, privacy-masked artifacts, hashes, and package manifests.\n- `video_library_governance`: ingest, index, embed, check storage, or manage video assets.\n- `camera_health_operations`: diagnose online status, black screen, blur, occlusion, freeze, corruption, or view shift.\n- `cross_video_investigation`: compare, correlate, or track across cameras and time windows.\n- `business_scenario_orchestration`: translate role-based requests into one of the above chains.\n- `development_test`: benchmark or compare retrieval/embedding behavior only when the user explicitly asks for testing or development.\n\n## Output Contract\n\nReturn or preserve JSON-compatible fields:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"success\",\n  \"request\": \"\",\n  \"mode\": \"business_operation | development_test\",\n  \"capability\": \"\",\n  \"business_scenario\": \"\",\n  \"recommended_skill_chain\": [],\n  \"execution_plan\": [],\n  \"expected_deliverables\": [],\n  \"embedding_attempt_required\": false,\n  \"embedding_failure_policy\": \"keep_source_and_report_partial_success | null\",\n  \"source_index\": \"citybrain-video-library | null\",\n  \"embedding_target_index\": \"citybrain-video-library | null\",\n  \"embedding_storage_mode\": \"in_place | null\",\n  \"missing_fields\": [],\n  \"follow_up_question\": null,\n  \"guardrails\": [],\n  \"requires_confirmation\": false,\n  \"requires_human_review\": false,\n  \"capability_gap\": null\n}\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Do not execute downstream atomic skills until the plan is clear.\n- Do not create new code to bypass an unsupported operation.\n- Do not perform destructive video-library management without explicit confirmation.\n- Do not produce legal, enforcement, or emergency conclusions without evidence references and review status.\n- For ingestion aggregation, use `success` when source and vector writes succeed, `partial_success` when the source write succeeds but vector generation fails, and `failed` when source ingestion fails.\n- If the plan includes `follow_up_question`, the whole visible response must be exactly that question. Preserve any ingestion JSON template already included in it, but do not append additional preamble, alternatives, or guidance, and do not run downstream tools first.\n- If a plan has `capability_gap`, do not implement new functionality. State the nearest supported workflow or ask the single `follow_up_question` when present.\n","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"read_file","id":"3fc1bf5e-3e54-469b-aa13-5911307f2b15","tool_call_id":"call_c80253603ab54078a911657d","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"先运行编排脚本，获取执行计划：\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":160,"prompt_tokens":16447,"total_tokens":16607,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":34,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":160},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":16447}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-cfb19e7b-f0f1-964c-a605-fa6fcf10b43f","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1c-148a-7711-9080-0323b5ccb7a8-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"bash","args":{"command":"cd /mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence && python scripts/run.py --request \"分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线\" --output /tmp/cvi_plan.json 2>&1","description":"运行 city-video-intelligence 编排脚本获取执行计划"},"id":"call_c14bde36053f4acaaa471be6","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":16447,"output_tokens":160,"total_tokens":16607,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":34}}},{"content":"{\n  \"skill\": \"city-video-intelligence\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"status\": \"success\",\n  \"request\": \"分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线\",\n  \"role\": null,\n  \"mode\": \"business_operation\",\n  \"capability\": \"single_video_event_understanding\",\n  \"capability_label\": \"单视频事件理解\",\n  \"business_scenario\": \"generic_video_intelligence\",\n  \"business_scenario_label\": \"generic_video_intelligence\",\n  \"recommended_skill_chain\": [\n    \"single-video-event-analysis\"\n  ],\n  \"execution_plan\": [\n    {\n      \"step\": \"1\",\n      \"skill\": \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n      \"action\": \"Load single-video-event-analysis and inspect frames for visible event evidence.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"expected_deliverables\": [\n    \"视觉时间线\",\n    \"事件候选\",\n    \"证据帧\",\n    \"置信度\",\n    \"人工复核状态\"\n  ],\n  \"embedding_attempt_required\": false,\n  \"embedding_failure_policy\": null,\n  \"source_index\": null,\n  \"embedding_target_index\": null,\n  \"embedding_storage_mode\": null,\n  \"missing_fields\": [],\n  \"follow_up_question\": null,\n  \"guardrails\": [\n    \"Do not write ad hoc code for this business request.\",\n    \"Load each downstream skill's SKILL.md before executing its script.\",\n    \"Return capability_gap instead of implementing missing functionality.\",\n    \"If follow_up_question is present, stop immediately and make the whole visible response exactly that question.\",\n    \"If a downstream video skill fails, summarize the concrete failure and stop instead of debugging services.\",\n    \"Include evidence references and human-review status for high-risk or enforcement-sensitive conclusions.\"\n  ],\n  \"requires_confirmation\": false,\n  \"requires_human_review\": true,\n  \"capability_gap\": null\n}","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"bash","id":"43cfe2b8-8cef-4d24-a2e4-9aa9be240d5d","tool_call_id":"call_c14bde36053f4acaaa471be6","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"编排计划已确认，需要加载 `single-video-event-analysis` 技能进行事件分析。\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":139,"prompt_tokens":17036,"total_tokens":17175,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":22,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":139},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":17036}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-b59236ba-1049-9d6e-bde4-0a245c06dd5c","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1c-21b0-7121-beb5-1fb87461257b-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"invoke_skill","args":{"input_envelope":"{\"event_types\": [\"fight\", \"fall\"], \"output_format\": \"timeline\", \"video_path\": \"/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4\"}","mode":"prepare","skill_name":"single-video-event-analysis"},"id":"call_8bbdc176c5c340ba90599610","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":17036,"output_tokens":139,"total_tokens":17175,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":22}}},{"content":"{\n  \"status\": \"prepared\",\n  \"skill_name\": \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n  \"input_envelope\": {\n    \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n    \"request_id\": \"7e5b647d-d87f-4d03-a927-e4d6760e0dd0\",\n    \"skill_name\": \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n    \"scenario\": \"video_surveillance\",\n    \"capability\": \"skill_invocation\",\n    \"query\": {\n      \"raw\": \"<system_reminder>\\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\\n<hidden_step source=\\\"intent_recognition\\\" title=\\\"意图识别\\\">\\n改写后的任务：场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance\\n识别场景：视频监控 (video_surveillance)；场景模式：single；候选场景：video_surveillance\\n任务切分：\\n- 请分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。\\n任务规划：\\n1. 读取/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4视频文件，校验文件元数据与编码格式，按预设帧率执行流媒体解码与关键帧抽样，输出可供下游模型调用的标准化图像序列与对应时间戳映射表。\\n2. 基于视频监控场景的行为识别能力，对抽样帧序列应用人体姿态估计与动作分类模型，聚焦“打架”与“摔倒”两类目标特征进行时空关联分析，设定置信度阈值进行初筛，输出包含事件类型、预估起止时间及置信度分数的候选事件清单。\\n3. 依据运动轨迹突变程度与连续帧状态一致性规则，对候选事件清单进行二次交叉研判与噪声过滤，明确异常动作判定的关键指标与排除口径，输出经算法复核确认的高置信度事件区间数据集。\\n4. 将最终确认的事件区间按时间先后逻辑进行序列化编排，整合事件类型、发生时长、画面关键特征摘要及原始视频溯源链接，生成结构化时间线报告供后续业务调度使用。\\n场景任务：\\n- video_surveillance: 我将分析/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4中的打架和摔倒情况，并以时间线形式输出结果。；参数：{'视频对象': '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4', '监控目标': '打架、摔倒', '输出形式': '时间线'}\\n已提取参数：{'视频对象': '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4', '监控目标': '打架、摔倒', '输出形式': '时间线'}\\n任务提示：\\n- 提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧\\n- 提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等\\n- 提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口\\n- 提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要\\n</hidden_step>\\n</system_reminder>\"\n    },\n    \"inputs\": {\n      \"parameters\": {}\n    },\n    \"routing\": {\n      \"selected_skill\": \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n      \"allowed_skills\": [\n        \"analyze-video\",\n        \"batch-video-ingestion\",\n        \"camera-health-check\",\n        \"city-video-intelligence\",\n        \"duplicate-event-merge\",\n        \"evidence-package-generation\",\n        \"evidence-snapshot\",\n        \"ffmpeg-utils\",\n        \"frame-sampling\",\n        \"human-review-routing\",\n        \"object-detection\",\n        \"object-statistics\",\n        \"object-tracking\",\n        \"privacy-masking\",\n        \"roi-mapping\",\n        \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n        \"video-embedding-index\",\n        \"video-object-analytics\",\n        \"video-search\",\n        \"video-segment-extraction\",\n        \"video-stream-ingestion\"\n      ],\n      \"selection_owner\": \"lead_agent\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"legacy_invocation\": {\n    \"skill_dir\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis\",\n    \"skill_file\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis/SKILL.md\",\n    \"container_skill_file\": \"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis/SKILL.md\",\n    \"selected_data_sources\": [],\n    \"argv\": [],\n    \"env\": {},\n    \"parameters\": {},\n    \"working_directory\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis\",\n    \"adapter_note\": \"Load the returned container_skill_file, follow its SKILL.md workflow, and use selected_data_sources/parameters as the legacy inputs.\"\n  },\n  \"next_steps\": [\n    \"Read container_skill_file before executing the Skill workflow.\",\n    \"Use selected_data_sources and parameters as the legacy inputs.\",\n    \"After execution, call invoke_skill again with mode='wrap_output' to produce SkillResult.\"\n  ]\n}","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"invoke_skill","id":"b0148bae-c034-48fe-a3bf-41fc27817f58","tool_call_id":"call_8bbdc176c5c340ba90599610","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":84,"prompt_tokens":18356,"total_tokens":18440,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":19,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":84},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":18356}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-9ce67b55-cff3-99f2-85d3-a7aeb8985d99","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1c-2b40-74b0-aa32-e1126c4daf8c-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"description":"读取 single-video-event-analysis 技能的工作流说明","path":"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis/SKILL.md"},"id":"call_857292050c754af6bc99d80b","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":18356,"output_tokens":84,"total_tokens":18440,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":19}}},{"content":"---\nname: single-video-event-analysis\ndescription: Analyze one local monitoring video for incidents after city-video-intelligence has routed the request, by extracting timestamped frames and having the LLM review visible evidence. Use for fight, fall, traffic accident, congestion, crowd gathering, smoke/fire, intrusion, illegal occupation, or other abnormal events. For direct user monitoring-video event questions, load city-video-intelligence first. This skill is the only custom event-detection entrypoint; YOLO/object detection may be used only as optional object context and must not decide event semantics.\n---\n\n# Single Video Event Analysis\n\n## Purpose\n\nUse this skill when the user wants to know what happened in a monitoring video.\nEvent detection is based on extracted frames and LLM visual review, not YOLO labels,\ntracking duration, ROI geometry, or rule templates alone.\n\n## Business Orchestration Gate\n\nIf this skill is loaded for a direct user monitoring-video request and no `city-video-intelligence` plan has already been executed in the current turn, load `city-video-intelligence` first and run its router script with the raw user request. Continue here only when that plan recommends `single-video-event-analysis`.\n\nDo not edit this skill's files or scripts during business execution. If the script fails, report the concrete failure and stop unless the user explicitly asked for debugging or implementation.\n\n## Execution Priority\n\n1. Use `write_file` to create a small input JSON file, then run `scripts/run.py` with `--input <file>`. Do not use shell heredocs or pass an inline JSON string to `--input`.\n2. Read the returned `review_manifest_uri` and use the listed `frames` as the review set.\n3. Inspect only the listed review frames in chronological order. Default maximum is 8 images.\n4. Read `all_frames_uri` or inspect denser frames only if a reviewed frame visibly suggests a possible event or is too ambiguous to classify.\n5. Produce the final event analysis from visible evidence and stop. Do not keep browsing frames after the conclusion is clear.\n\n## Atomic CLI\n\n```bash\npython single-video-event-analysis/scripts/run.py \\\n  --input <input.json> \\\n  --config <config.json> \\\n  --output <prepared_manifest.json>\n```\n\nUseful fields in `input.json`:\n\n- `video_path`, `file_path`, `raw_segment_uri`, or `video`\n- `camera_id`\n- `target_events`\n- `output_dir`\n- `coarse_fps`, `dense_fps`, `scene_threshold`, `dense_window`, `max_frames`\n\nFor ordinary business questions, omit `max_frames` so the script default samples across the whole video and exposes only 8 review frames. Do not use `max_frames` as the review-image limit. Do not rerun the script after a successful result.\n\n## Review Rules\n\n- Only report events that are visible in the sampled frames.\n- Use `unknown` or `requires_review=true` when evidence is blurry, occluded, sparse, or ambiguous.\n- Use at least two timestamps for temporal claims unless a single frame clearly shows aftermath, smoke, fire, a crash scene, or a fallen person.\n- Do not let YOLO output decide events. YOLO can only provide optional object context such as \"person\", \"car\", or \"truck\".\n- Include negative evidence when useful, such as \"no visible collision before 00:12\".\n- Never include internal thinking markers such as `<think>` or `</think>` in the final user-visible response.\n- If a draft answer contains hidden reasoning before a `</think>` token, discard that hidden text and answer only with the event result and visible evidence summary.\n- For negative findings, phrase the conclusion as evidence-bound, such as \"未在抽样审阅帧中发现交通事故迹象\", unless the reviewed evidence covers the full incident window.\n\n## Output Schema\n\nReturn a JSON-compatible result with:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"video\": {},\n  \"visual_timeline\": [\n    {\n      \"time\": \"00:00:12.000\",\n      \"frame_id\": \"frame_000012000ms\",\n      \"observation\": \"Visible subjects, actions, spatial relations, and scene state.\",\n      \"uncertainty\": \"Optional ambiguity note.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"events\": [\n    {\n      \"event_id\": \"EVT_...\",\n      \"event_type\": \"fight | fall_down | traffic_accident | traffic_congestion | crowd_gathering | smoke_or_fire | intrusion | illegal_occupation | other_abnormal_event | unknown\",\n      \"start_time\": \"00:00:10.000\",\n      \"end_time\": \"00:00:18.000\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.0,\n      \"severity\": \"low | medium | high\",\n      \"evidence_frame_ids\": [],\n      \"reason\": \"Concrete visible evidence and uncertainty.\",\n      \"requires_review\": true\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"Short human-readable summary.\",\n  \"warnings\": []\n}\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Do not call legacy rule-based event skills. They have been removed from this bundle.\n- Do not infer off-camera causes.\n- Do not fabricate exact counts when the frame only supports a range.\n","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"read_file","id":"86a7fa18-c416-43d5-945c-091beacd9334","tool_call_id":"call_857292050c754af6bc99d80b","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"技能已加载。现在创建输入文件并执行分析脚本：\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":133,"prompt_tokens":19580,"total_tokens":19713,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":52,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":133},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":19580}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-9ac8d936-a82f-9161-8b03-09dabb1f1512","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1c-32fb-7ea3-87cd-a06fc3f58e4a-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"bash","args":{"command":"ls -la /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 2>&1","description":"检查视频文件是否存在"},"id":"call_178103da008548158153152c","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":19580,"output_tokens":133,"total_tokens":19713,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":52}}},{"content":"ls: cannot access '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4': No such file or directory","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"bash","id":"032f20c9-8270-4cde-af89-2bed16ce13ff","tool_call_id":"call_178103da008548158153152c","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"视频文件不存在。让我先确认一下上传目录中是否有其他视频文件：\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":142,"prompt_tokens":19700,"total_tokens":19842,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":61,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":142},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":19700}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-f4e16b16-cc05-9e91-ae0b-38dd265cee1f","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1c-3dc6-74a0-8d6b-a79b6e7f4d88-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"bash","args":{"command":"ls -la /mnt/user-data/uploads/ 2>&1 | head -30","description":"检查上传目录中的文件列表"},"id":"call_9e5d310194d54b4fb603364c","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":19700,"output_tokens":142,"total_tokens":19842,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":61}}}],"viewed_images":{},"thread_data":{"workspace_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/eeda22b6-e72a-4ec4-922a-abab62a9f8fd/user-data/workspace","uploads_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/eeda22b6-e72a-4ec4-922a-abab62a9f8fd/user-data/uploads","outputs_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/eeda22b6-e72a-4ec4-922a-abab62a9f8fd/user-data/outputs"},"title":"Surveillance Fight and Fall Timeline","raw_messages":[{"content":"请分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"34ad83b1-a1de-4e51-bbd5-2b2fe8512eb1"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze-video</name>\n      <description>专业视频抽帧与取证准备技能。支持场景检测、多阶段帧提取和 metadata 生成，供 single-video-event-analysis 做 LLM 审帧使用；本 skill 不再作为最终事件检测入口。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/analyze-video/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>batch-video-ingestion</name>\n      <description>Batch ingest local monitoring videos into the Elasticsearch video library after city-video-intelligence has routed the request, with metadata, sampled-frame object summaries, and searchable documents. For direct user video ingestion, ingest-and-embed, Elasticsearch, StreetModel, or business video-library requests, load city-video-intelligence first. Use this atomic skill when Codex already has a clear ingestion plan, video directory, video manifest, camera_id, or multiple video files to index for later retrieval and statistics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/batch-video-ingestion/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>camera-health-check</name>\n      <description>Check video monitoring camera quality from sampled frames and return health status before downstream event generation. Use when Codex has camera_id and frames and needs to gate or downgrade event confidence for offline, unavailable, degraded, black-screen, blurred, occluded, frozen, corrupted, or shifted camera feeds.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/camera-health-check/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>city-video-intelligence</name>\n      <description>Business orchestration for city video intelligence requests. Use when users ask for monitoring video search, semantic video retrieval, event review, object statistics, evidence packages, video ingestion, camera health operations, cross-camera analysis, or role-based scenarios such as traffic police, property security, urban management, emergency management, or legal evidence preparation. Also use it when the user asks what the current data and skills can or cannot support (capability-boundary questions) — it answers with an explicit capability_gap instead of guessing. This skill maps business intent to existing custom video skills and prevents ad hoc code generation unless the user explicitly asks for development or testing.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>duplicate-event-merge</name>\n      <description>Merge duplicate video event candidates from the same camera, event type, ROI, evidence frames, or overlapping time window. Use after single-video-event-analysis or batch video analysis when Codex has a list of Event Candidate records and needs canonical events plus duplicate mappings.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/duplicate-event-merge/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>evidence-package-generation</name>\n      <description>Generate an evidence package manifest for indexed monitoring videos or event/search results, including snapshot evidence and optional short video clips. Use when Codex needs a package_id, manifest URI, evidence items, hashes, and reusable evidence artifacts.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/evidence-package-generation/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>evidence-snapshot</name>\n      <description>Generate snapshot evidence for video monitoring event candidates. Use when Codex has an event, event_id, evidence_frame_ids, image_uri, or frame list and needs a snapshot URI, SHA-256 integrity hash, created_at timestamp, privacy masking status, and Evidence schema output.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/evidence-snapshot/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>ffmpeg-utils</name>\n      <description>视频处理工具集，支持视频截取和关键帧提取。常用于将监控视频剪辑为证据片段。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/ffmpeg-utils/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>frame-sampling</name>\n      <description>Sample structured frames from an existing video file. Use when Codex has video_path, file_path, raw_segment_uri, camera_id, sampling_strategy, capture_seconds, or provided frame records and needs stable Frame schema outputs. This skill exposes OpenCV-backed real video frame extraction.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/frame-sampling/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>human-review-routing</name>\n      <description>Decide whether video monitoring event candidates require manual review. Use after event generation and evidence creation when Codex has event confidence, event_type, review_threshold, camera_health, high_risk_event_types, newly added camera signals, or enforcement-impact flags and needs review queue routing.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>object-detection</name>\n      <description>Detect visible objects in sampled video frames and return standard Detection schema only. Use when Codex needs YOLO labels, confidences, and bounding boxes for people, vehicles, or COCO objects. Do not use this skill to infer events, abnormal behavior, accidents, fights, falls, congestion, intrusion, smoke/fire, or business semantics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/object-detection/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>object-statistics</name>\n      <description>Compute object statistics for monitoring videos from Elasticsearch video-library records or local detections/tracks JSON. Use when Codex needs counts by label, camera, time bucket, or movement state.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/object-statistics/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>object-tracking</name>\n      <description>Track detected objects across video frames and return Track schema for object analytics only. Use when Codex has frame-level detections and needs stable track ids, trajectories, duration, last bbox, movement state, confidence, and evidence frame ids. Do not use this skill to infer video events or abnormal behavior.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/object-tracking/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>privacy-masking</name>\n      <description>Mask sensitive visual data in video evidence such as faces, license plates, phone numbers, and doorplates. Use when Codex has an evidence image URI and explicit sensitive_regions bbox coordinates, or privacy_masking config and needs a masked URI before exposing snapshots or clips externally. This skill exposes OpenCV image read/write and Gaussian blur masking for real files.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/privacy-masking/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>roi-mapping</name>\n      <description>Match detections or tracks against configured camera ROI polygons for geometric object analytics. Use when Codex has camera_id plus tracks or objects and needs point containment or bbox overlap matches for configured areas. Do not use this skill to decide event semantics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/roi-mapping/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>single-video-event-analysis</name>\n      <description>Analyze one local monitoring video for incidents after city-video-intelligence has routed the request, by extracting timestamped frames and having the LLM review visible evidence. Use for fight, fall, traffic accident, congestion, crowd gathering, smoke/fire, intrusion, illegal occupation, or other abnormal events. For direct user monitoring-video event questions, load city-video-intelligence first. This skill is the only custom event-detection entrypoint; YOLO/object detection may be used only as optional object context and must not decide event semantics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-embedding-index</name>\n      <description>Generate text embeddings or StreetModel sampled-frame image embeddings for video-library documents after city-video-intelligence has routed the request. Only enrich citybrain-video-library in place. For direct user StreetModel, ingest-and-embed, semantic retrieval, benchmark, or keyword-vs-vector requests, load city-video-intelligence first.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-embedding-index/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-object-analytics</name>\n      <description>Deterministic structured entrypoint for local-video object detection and cross-frame tracking. Use for direct requests to count visible people, vehicles, or other objects, or to track them across frames. The dedicated video_object_analytics tool owns all CLI parameters, model configuration, persistent paths, and downstream skill order.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-object-analytics/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-search</name>\n      <description>Search indexed monitoring videos from text, images, structured filters, or precomputed vectors. Use for keyword retrieval, LLM-optimized text-to-video semantic retrieval, combined keyword/vector search, or image-to-video similarity search against StreetModel/Qwen3-VL video vectors.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-search/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-segment-extraction</name>\n      <description>Extract playable short video evidence clips around event times. Use when Codex has event_id, camera_id, raw_segment_uri, event_time, event_elapsed_seconds, pre_seconds, or post_seconds and needs an MP4 clip URI plus clip time range. This skill exposes FFmpeg-backed clipping for real local videos and memory-backed synthetic clips for tests.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-segment-extraction/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-stream-ingestion</name>\n      <description>Normalize an existing local video file after city-video-intelligence has routed a video-library or analysis request, returning raw segment/session metadata such as duration, resolution, frame rate, codec, and session times. Use it for any \"read this video's duration / resolution / fps / codec / metadata\" or \"turn this video into a standard analysis input\" request instead of running ffprobe by hand. For direct user ingestion, Elasticsearch, StreetModel, search, statistics, evidence, or camera-health requests, load city-video-intelligence first. Use this atomic skill when Codex already has a clear plan and a local MP4/MOV/AVI/MKV file before frame sampling.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-stream-ingestion/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"b1adea96-db0b-4fa5-b74a-91a2e26e870e"},{"content":"<system_reminder>\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\n<hidden_step source=\"intent_recognition\" title=\"意图识别\">\n改写后的任务：场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance\n识别场景：视频监控 (video_surveillance)；场景模式：single；候选场景：video_surveillance\n任务切分：\n- 请分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。\n任务规划：\n1. 读取/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4视频文件，校验文件元数据与编码格式，按预设帧率执行流媒体解码与关键帧抽样，输出可供下游模型调用的标准化图像序列与对应时间戳映射表。\n2. 基于视频监控场景的行为识别能力，对抽样帧序列应用人体姿态估计与动作分类模型，聚焦“打架”与“摔倒”两类目标特征进行时空关联分析，设定置信度阈值进行初筛，输出包含事件类型、预估起止时间及置信度分数的候选事件清单。\n3. 依据运动轨迹突变程度与连续帧状态一致性规则，对候选事件清单进行二次交叉研判与噪声过滤，明确异常动作判定的关键指标与排除口径，输出经算法复核确认的高置信度事件区间数据集。\n4. 将最终确认的事件区间按时间先后逻辑进行序列化编排，整合事件类型、发生时长、画面关键特征摘要及原始视频溯源链接，生成结构化时间线报告供后续业务调度使用。\n场景任务：\n- video_surveillance: 我将分析/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4中的打架和摔倒情况，并以时间线形式输出结果。；参数：{'视频对象': '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4', '监控目标': '打架、摔倒', '输出形式': '时间线'}\n已提取参数：{'视频对象': '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4', '监控目标': '打架、摔倒', '输出形式': '时间线'}\n任务提示：\n- 提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧\n- 提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等\n- 提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口\n- 提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要\n</hidden_step>\n</system_reminder>","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"todo_routing_guidance","id":"d96bf895-4041-4819-9c0a-9b891870cf3d"},{"content":"这是一个视频监控事件分析任务，我先加载编排技能，然后进行打架/摔倒检测。\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":200,"prompt_tokens":13292,"total_tokens":13492,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":84,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":200},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":13292}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-14a7964f-a96c-99df-8a17-f1e11ac5dcce","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1b-87cf-7ff3-b998-ba08c07981bb-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"invoke_skill","args":{"skill_name":"city-video-intelligence","mode":"prepare","input_envelope":"{\"video_path\": \"/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4\", \"event_types\": [\"fight\", \"fall\"], \"output_format\": \"timeline\"}"},"id":"call_6ca3ad4f27f24339b0460ebf","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":13292,"output_tokens":200,"total_tokens":13492,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":84}}},{"content":"{\n  \"status\": \"prepared\",\n  \"skill_name\": \"city-video-intelligence\",\n  \"input_envelope\": {\n    \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n    \"request_id\": \"95b943f1-f783-4352-8556-7f3398b89bdc\",\n    \"skill_name\": \"city-video-intelligence\",\n    \"scenario\": \"video_surveillance\",\n    \"capability\": \"skill_invocation\",\n    \"query\": {\n      \"raw\": \"<system_reminder>\\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\\n<hidden_step source=\\\"intent_recognition\\\" title=\\\"意图识别\\\">\\n改写后的任务：场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance\\n识别场景：视频监控 (video_surveillance)；场景模式：single；候选场景：video_surveillance\\n任务切分：\\n- 请分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。\\n任务规划：\\n1. 读取/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4视频文件，校验文件元数据与编码格式，按预设帧率执行流媒体解码与关键帧抽样，输出可供下游模型调用的标准化图像序列与对应时间戳映射表。\\n2. 基于视频监控场景的行为识别能力，对抽样帧序列应用人体姿态估计与动作分类模型，聚焦“打架”与“摔倒”两类目标特征进行时空关联分析，设定置信度阈值进行初筛，输出包含事件类型、预估起止时间及置信度分数的候选事件清单。\\n3. 依据运动轨迹突变程度与连续帧状态一致性规则，对候选事件清单进行二次交叉研判与噪声过滤，明确异常动作判定的关键指标与排除口径，输出经算法复核确认的高置信度事件区间数据集。\\n4. 将最终确认的事件区间按时间先后逻辑进行序列化编排，整合事件类型、发生时长、画面关键特征摘要及原始视频溯源链接，生成结构化时间线报告供后续业务调度使用。\\n场景任务：\\n- video_surveillance: 我将分析/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4中的打架和摔倒情况，并以时间线形式输出结果。；参数：{'视频对象': '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4', '监控目标': '打架、摔倒', '输出形式': '时间线'}\\n已提取参数：{'视频对象': '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4', '监控目标': '打架、摔倒', '输出形式': '时间线'}\\n任务提示：\\n- 提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧\\n- 提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等\\n- 提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口\\n- 提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要\\n</hidden_step>\\n</system_reminder>\"\n    },\n    \"inputs\": {\n      \"parameters\": {}\n    },\n    \"routing\": {\n      \"selected_skill\": \"city-video-intelligence\",\n      \"allowed_skills\": [\n        \"analyze-video\",\n        \"batch-video-ingestion\",\n        \"camera-health-check\",\n        \"city-video-intelligence\",\n        \"duplicate-event-merge\",\n        \"evidence-package-generation\",\n        \"evidence-snapshot\",\n        \"ffmpeg-utils\",\n        \"frame-sampling\",\n        \"human-review-routing\",\n        \"object-detection\",\n        \"object-statistics\",\n        \"object-tracking\",\n        \"privacy-masking\",\n        \"roi-mapping\",\n        \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n        \"video-embedding-index\",\n        \"video-object-analytics\",\n        \"video-search\",\n        \"video-segment-extraction\",\n        \"video-stream-ingestion\"\n      ],\n      \"selection_owner\": \"lead_agent\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"legacy_invocation\": {\n    \"skill_dir\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence\",\n    \"skill_file\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence/SKILL.md\",\n    \"container_skill_file\": \"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence/SKILL.md\",\n    \"selected_data_sources\": [],\n    \"argv\": [],\n    \"env\": {},\n    \"parameters\": {},\n    \"working_directory\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence\",\n    \"adapter_note\": \"Load the returned container_skill_file, follow its SKILL.md workflow, and use selected_data_sources/parameters as the legacy inputs.\"\n  },\n  \"next_steps\": [\n    \"Read container_skill_file before executing the Skill workflow.\",\n    \"Use selected_data_sources and parameters as the legacy inputs.\",\n    \"After execution, call invoke_skill again with mode='wrap_output' to produce SkillResult.\"\n  ]\n}","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"invoke_skill","id":"869d54da-5978-4a9f-b33f-faa495d3dc00","tool_call_id":"call_6ca3ad4f27f24339b0460ebf","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":83,"prompt_tokens":14617,"total_tokens":14700,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":17,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":83},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":14617}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-99326868-af9b-9ea0-8d5c-05e40f6c0906","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1b-fd44-7e62-bfa0-cfcd3b7acf64-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"description":"读取 city-video-intelligence 技能的工作流说明","path":"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence/SKILL.md"},"id":"call_c80253603ab54078a911657d","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":14617,"output_tokens":83,"total_tokens":14700,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":17}}},{"content":"---\nname: city-video-intelligence\ndescription: Business orchestration for city video intelligence requests. Use when users ask for monitoring video search, semantic video retrieval, event review, object statistics, evidence packages, video ingestion, camera health operations, cross-camera analysis, or role-based scenarios such as traffic police, property security, urban management, emergency management, or legal evidence preparation. Also use it when the user asks what the current data and skills can or cannot support (capability-boundary questions) — it answers with an explicit capability_gap instead of guessing. This skill maps business intent to existing custom video skills and prevents ad hoc code generation unless the user explicitly asks for development or testing.\n---\n\n# City Video Intelligence Orchestration\n\n## Overview\n\nUse this skill as the business layer above the existing video-monitoring atomic skills. It classifies a user request, selects the right capability and scenario, returns the recommended skill chain, and states the expected business deliverable. Use it for direct user tasks as well as planning questions.\n\nThis skill is not a replacement for `video-search`, `single-video-event-analysis`, `object-statistics`, `evidence-package-generation`, `batch-video-ingestion`, `camera-health-check`, or related atomic skills. It tells the agent which of those existing skills to use and when to stop for human confirmation.\n\n## Execution Priority\n\n1. Run `scripts/run.py` with the user's raw request to produce a structured orchestration plan. This is mandatory before any clarification question, except destructive operations that require confirmation.\n2. Read `references/capability-map.md` only when the request is ambiguous, role-based, multi-step, or asks about available capabilities.\n3. Follow the returned `recommended_skill_chain` by loading each downstream skill's `SKILL.md` before running its script.\n4. Return business-facing results: matched capability, scenario, execution plan, deliverables, risks, and required confirmations.\n5. If the plan contains a non-empty `follow_up_question`, stop immediately and make the whole visible response exactly that question as plain assistant text. For ingestion requests, preserve the returned JSON template verbatim. Do not inspect datasets, probe services, load downstream skills, or call `ask_clarification`.\n\n## Atomic CLI\n\n```bash\npython city-video-intelligence/scripts/run.py \\\n  --request \"我是交警队的，需要调取大成路路口今天上午 8-10 点的监控\" \\\n  --output <plan.json>\n```\n\nParameters: `--request`, `--role`, `--output`, `--format`.\n\n## Business Mode Rules\n\n- Do not write ad hoc Python, JavaScript, SQL, or shell code for business requests.\n- Use existing skill scripts and documented workflows. If existing skills cannot satisfy the request, return a `capability_gap` and ask for authorization before implementation work.\n- Treat destructive operations such as deleting indexed videos, rewriting shared indices, or purging test data as requiring explicit confirmation.\n- Treat event conclusions as evidence-bound. If video evidence is missing, blurry, occluded, sparse, or ambiguous, return `requires_human_review=true`.\n- Do not let object detection alone decide event semantics. Use it only as supporting context.\n- For evidence package requests, do not run event analysis merely to invent an event. If the user provides an event time or time range, package that range. If the event time is missing, ask for it or return a plan with the missing input.\n- For development or benchmark requests, use provided test videos, indexes, or query terms. If no test data is available, return `capability_gap` or ask for the missing dataset before running lower-level tools.\n- When asking for missing information, ask only one concrete question. The ingestion-format template returned by the router is the sole exception: show it verbatim. Do not add any text before or after the returned question.\n- If a downstream video skill returns `status: failed`, summarize that failure and stop. Do not debug services or probe ports unless the user explicitly asks for debugging.\n- Attempt StreetModel sampled-frame image embedding for every ingestion request. Always run `video-stream-ingestion`, then `batch-video-ingestion` in metadata-only mode, then `video-embedding-index` with `embedding_provider=streetmodel`, `video_preprocess=image_frames`, and in-place storage. Do not require a StreetModel-visible video mount for the default ingestion path.\n- Store source metadata and StreetModel vector fields in the same `citybrain-video-library` document. Use partial ES updates for embedding enrichment; never replace the full source document with a compact vector copy.\n- Allow video ingestion, search, statistics, evidence lookup, and embedding tools to access only `citybrain-video-library`. Reject every other video index before making an Elasticsearch request.\n- For video search, route image input to direct image-vector retrieval. Route text input to keyword retrieval plus an LLM-optimized text-to-video vector query, then use the search skill's fused ranking.\n- If source ingestion succeeds and vector generation fails, keep the source-index document and return partial success. Report `overall_status=partial_success`, `source_ingestion_status=success`, `vector_status=failed`, and the concrete embedding error. Never roll back or delete the source document.\n- Once the orchestration plan or requested downstream result is available, stop calling tools and summarize the result.\n\n## Capability Families\n\nUse these families to classify requests before selecting downstream skills:\n\n- `video_asset_retrieval`: locate known videos or indexed clips by keyword, camera, place, time, object, or count condition.\n- `semantic_video_retrieval`: retrieve videos by natural-language visual meaning through StreetModel/vector search.\n- `single_video_event_understanding`: inspect one video and produce a timeline, event candidates, confidence, and review status.\n- `object_statistics`: count objects, group by time/camera/type, and summarize trends.\n- `evidence_preservation`: generate snapshots, clips, privacy-masked artifacts, hashes, and package manifests.\n- `video_library_governance`: ingest, index, embed, check storage, or manage video assets.\n- `camera_health_operations`: diagnose online status, black screen, blur, occlusion, freeze, corruption, or view shift.\n- `cross_video_investigation`: compare, correlate, or track across cameras and time windows.\n- `business_scenario_orchestration`: translate role-based requests into one of the above chains.\n- `development_test`: benchmark or compare retrieval/embedding behavior only when the user explicitly asks for testing or development.\n\n## Output Contract\n\nReturn or preserve JSON-compatible fields:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"success\",\n  \"request\": \"\",\n  \"mode\": \"business_operation | development_test\",\n  \"capability\": \"\",\n  \"business_scenario\": \"\",\n  \"recommended_skill_chain\": [],\n  \"execution_plan\": [],\n  \"expected_deliverables\": [],\n  \"embedding_attempt_required\": false,\n  \"embedding_failure_policy\": \"keep_source_and_report_partial_success | null\",\n  \"source_index\": \"citybrain-video-library | null\",\n  \"embedding_target_index\": \"citybrain-video-library | null\",\n  \"embedding_storage_mode\": \"in_place | null\",\n  \"missing_fields\": [],\n  \"follow_up_question\": null,\n  \"guardrails\": [],\n  \"requires_confirmation\": false,\n  \"requires_human_review\": false,\n  \"capability_gap\": null\n}\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Do not execute downstream atomic skills until the plan is clear.\n- Do not create new code to bypass an unsupported operation.\n- Do not perform destructive video-library management without explicit confirmation.\n- Do not produce legal, enforcement, or emergency conclusions without evidence references and review status.\n- For ingestion aggregation, use `success` when source and vector writes succeed, `partial_success` when the source write succeeds but vector generation fails, and `failed` when source ingestion fails.\n- If the plan includes `follow_up_question`, the whole visible response must be exactly that question. Preserve any ingestion JSON template already included in it, but do not append additional preamble, alternatives, or guidance, and do not run downstream tools first.\n- If a plan has `capability_gap`, do not implement new functionality. State the nearest supported workflow or ask the single `follow_up_question` when present.\n","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"read_file","id":"3fc1bf5e-3e54-469b-aa13-5911307f2b15","tool_call_id":"call_c80253603ab54078a911657d","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"先运行编排脚本，获取执行计划：\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":160,"prompt_tokens":16447,"total_tokens":16607,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":34,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":160},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":16447}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-cfb19e7b-f0f1-964c-a605-fa6fcf10b43f","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1c-148a-7711-9080-0323b5ccb7a8-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"bash","args":{"command":"cd /mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence && python scripts/run.py --request \"分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线\" --output /tmp/cvi_plan.json 2>&1","description":"运行 city-video-intelligence 编排脚本获取执行计划"},"id":"call_c14bde36053f4acaaa471be6","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":16447,"output_tokens":160,"total_tokens":16607,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":34}}},{"content":"{\n  \"skill\": \"city-video-intelligence\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"status\": \"success\",\n  \"request\": \"分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线\",\n  \"role\": null,\n  \"mode\": \"business_operation\",\n  \"capability\": \"single_video_event_understanding\",\n  \"capability_label\": \"单视频事件理解\",\n  \"business_scenario\": \"generic_video_intelligence\",\n  \"business_scenario_label\": \"generic_video_intelligence\",\n  \"recommended_skill_chain\": [\n    \"single-video-event-analysis\"\n  ],\n  \"execution_plan\": [\n    {\n      \"step\": \"1\",\n      \"skill\": \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n      \"action\": \"Load single-video-event-analysis and inspect frames for visible event evidence.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"expected_deliverables\": [\n    \"视觉时间线\",\n    \"事件候选\",\n    \"证据帧\",\n    \"置信度\",\n    \"人工复核状态\"\n  ],\n  \"embedding_attempt_required\": false,\n  \"embedding_failure_policy\": null,\n  \"source_index\": null,\n  \"embedding_target_index\": null,\n  \"embedding_storage_mode\": null,\n  \"missing_fields\": [],\n  \"follow_up_question\": null,\n  \"guardrails\": [\n    \"Do not write ad hoc code for this business request.\",\n    \"Load each downstream skill's SKILL.md before executing its script.\",\n    \"Return capability_gap instead of implementing missing functionality.\",\n    \"If follow_up_question is present, stop immediately and make the whole visible response exactly that question.\",\n    \"If a downstream video skill fails, summarize the concrete failure and stop instead of debugging services.\",\n    \"Include evidence references and human-review status for high-risk or enforcement-sensitive conclusions.\"\n  ],\n  \"requires_confirmation\": false,\n  \"requires_human_review\": true,\n  \"capability_gap\": null\n}","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"bash","id":"43cfe2b8-8cef-4d24-a2e4-9aa9be240d5d","tool_call_id":"call_c14bde36053f4acaaa471be6","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"编排计划已确认，需要加载 `single-video-event-analysis` 技能进行事件分析。\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":139,"prompt_tokens":17036,"total_tokens":17175,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":22,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":139},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":17036}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-b59236ba-1049-9d6e-bde4-0a245c06dd5c","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1c-21b0-7121-beb5-1fb87461257b-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"invoke_skill","args":{"input_envelope":"{\"event_types\": [\"fight\", \"fall\"], \"output_format\": \"timeline\", \"video_path\": \"/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4\"}","mode":"prepare","skill_name":"single-video-event-analysis"},"id":"call_8bbdc176c5c340ba90599610","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":17036,"output_tokens":139,"total_tokens":17175,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":22}}},{"content":"{\n  \"status\": \"prepared\",\n  \"skill_name\": \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n  \"input_envelope\": {\n    \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n    \"request_id\": \"7e5b647d-d87f-4d03-a927-e4d6760e0dd0\",\n    \"skill_name\": \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n    \"scenario\": \"video_surveillance\",\n    \"capability\": \"skill_invocation\",\n    \"query\": {\n      \"raw\": \"<system_reminder>\\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\\n<hidden_step source=\\\"intent_recognition\\\" title=\\\"意图识别\\\">\\n改写后的任务：场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance\\n识别场景：视频监控 (video_surveillance)；场景模式：single；候选场景：video_surveillance\\n任务切分：\\n- 请分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。\\n任务规划：\\n1. 读取/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4视频文件，校验文件元数据与编码格式，按预设帧率执行流媒体解码与关键帧抽样，输出可供下游模型调用的标准化图像序列与对应时间戳映射表。\\n2. 基于视频监控场景的行为识别能力，对抽样帧序列应用人体姿态估计与动作分类模型，聚焦“打架”与“摔倒”两类目标特征进行时空关联分析，设定置信度阈值进行初筛，输出包含事件类型、预估起止时间及置信度分数的候选事件清单。\\n3. 依据运动轨迹突变程度与连续帧状态一致性规则，对候选事件清单进行二次交叉研判与噪声过滤，明确异常动作判定的关键指标与排除口径，输出经算法复核确认的高置信度事件区间数据集。\\n4. 将最终确认的事件区间按时间先后逻辑进行序列化编排，整合事件类型、发生时长、画面关键特征摘要及原始视频溯源链接，生成结构化时间线报告供后续业务调度使用。\\n场景任务：\\n- video_surveillance: 我将分析/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4中的打架和摔倒情况，并以时间线形式输出结果。；参数：{'视频对象': '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4', '监控目标': '打架、摔倒', '输出形式': '时间线'}\\n已提取参数：{'视频对象': '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4', '监控目标': '打架、摔倒', '输出形式': '时间线'}\\n任务提示：\\n- 提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧\\n- 提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等\\n- 提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口\\n- 提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要\\n</hidden_step>\\n</system_reminder>\"\n    },\n    \"inputs\": {\n      \"parameters\": {}\n    },\n    \"routing\": {\n      \"selected_skill\": \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n      \"allowed_skills\": [\n        \"analyze-video\",\n        \"batch-video-ingestion\",\n        \"camera-health-check\",\n        \"city-video-intelligence\",\n        \"duplicate-event-merge\",\n        \"evidence-package-generation\",\n        \"evidence-snapshot\",\n        \"ffmpeg-utils\",\n        \"frame-sampling\",\n        \"human-review-routing\",\n        \"object-detection\",\n        \"object-statistics\",\n        \"object-tracking\",\n        \"privacy-masking\",\n        \"roi-mapping\",\n        \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n        \"video-embedding-index\",\n        \"video-object-analytics\",\n        \"video-search\",\n        \"video-segment-extraction\",\n        \"video-stream-ingestion\"\n      ],\n      \"selection_owner\": \"lead_agent\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"legacy_invocation\": {\n    \"skill_dir\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis\",\n    \"skill_file\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis/SKILL.md\",\n    \"container_skill_file\": \"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis/SKILL.md\",\n    \"selected_data_sources\": [],\n    \"argv\": [],\n    \"env\": {},\n    \"parameters\": {},\n    \"working_directory\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis\",\n    \"adapter_note\": \"Load the returned container_skill_file, follow its SKILL.md workflow, and use selected_data_sources/parameters as the legacy inputs.\"\n  },\n  \"next_steps\": [\n    \"Read container_skill_file before executing the Skill workflow.\",\n    \"Use selected_data_sources and parameters as the legacy inputs.\",\n    \"After execution, call invoke_skill again with mode='wrap_output' to produce SkillResult.\"\n  ]\n}","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"invoke_skill","id":"b0148bae-c034-48fe-a3bf-41fc27817f58","tool_call_id":"call_8bbdc176c5c340ba90599610","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":84,"prompt_tokens":18356,"total_tokens":18440,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":19,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":84},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":18356}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-9ce67b55-cff3-99f2-85d3-a7aeb8985d99","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1c-2b40-74b0-aa32-e1126c4daf8c-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"description":"读取 single-video-event-analysis 技能的工作流说明","path":"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis/SKILL.md"},"id":"call_857292050c754af6bc99d80b","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":18356,"output_tokens":84,"total_tokens":18440,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":19}}},{"content":"---\nname: single-video-event-analysis\ndescription: Analyze one local monitoring video for incidents after city-video-intelligence has routed the request, by extracting timestamped frames and having the LLM review visible evidence. Use for fight, fall, traffic accident, congestion, crowd gathering, smoke/fire, intrusion, illegal occupation, or other abnormal events. For direct user monitoring-video event questions, load city-video-intelligence first. This skill is the only custom event-detection entrypoint; YOLO/object detection may be used only as optional object context and must not decide event semantics.\n---\n\n# Single Video Event Analysis\n\n## Purpose\n\nUse this skill when the user wants to know what happened in a monitoring video.\nEvent detection is based on extracted frames and LLM visual review, not YOLO labels,\ntracking duration, ROI geometry, or rule templates alone.\n\n## Business Orchestration Gate\n\nIf this skill is loaded for a direct user monitoring-video request and no `city-video-intelligence` plan has already been executed in the current turn, load `city-video-intelligence` first and run its router script with the raw user request. Continue here only when that plan recommends `single-video-event-analysis`.\n\nDo not edit this skill's files or scripts during business execution. If the script fails, report the concrete failure and stop unless the user explicitly asked for debugging or implementation.\n\n## Execution Priority\n\n1. Use `write_file` to create a small input JSON file, then run `scripts/run.py` with `--input <file>`. Do not use shell heredocs or pass an inline JSON string to `--input`.\n2. Read the returned `review_manifest_uri` and use the listed `frames` as the review set.\n3. Inspect only the listed review frames in chronological order. Default maximum is 8 images.\n4. Read `all_frames_uri` or inspect denser frames only if a reviewed frame visibly suggests a possible event or is too ambiguous to classify.\n5. Produce the final event analysis from visible evidence and stop. Do not keep browsing frames after the conclusion is clear.\n\n## Atomic CLI\n\n```bash\npython single-video-event-analysis/scripts/run.py \\\n  --input <input.json> \\\n  --config <config.json> \\\n  --output <prepared_manifest.json>\n```\n\nUseful fields in `input.json`:\n\n- `video_path`, `file_path`, `raw_segment_uri`, or `video`\n- `camera_id`\n- `target_events`\n- `output_dir`\n- `coarse_fps`, `dense_fps`, `scene_threshold`, `dense_window`, `max_frames`\n\nFor ordinary business questions, omit `max_frames` so the script default samples across the whole video and exposes only 8 review frames. Do not use `max_frames` as the review-image limit. Do not rerun the script after a successful result.\n\n## Review Rules\n\n- Only report events that are visible in the sampled frames.\n- Use `unknown` or `requires_review=true` when evidence is blurry, occluded, sparse, or ambiguous.\n- Use at least two timestamps for temporal claims unless a single frame clearly shows aftermath, smoke, fire, a crash scene, or a fallen person.\n- Do not let YOLO output decide events. YOLO can only provide optional object context such as \"person\", \"car\", or \"truck\".\n- Include negative evidence when useful, such as \"no visible collision before 00:12\".\n- Never include internal thinking markers such as `<think>` or `</think>` in the final user-visible response.\n- If a draft answer contains hidden reasoning before a `</think>` token, discard that hidden text and answer only with the event result and visible evidence summary.\n- For negative findings, phrase the conclusion as evidence-bound, such as \"未在抽样审阅帧中发现交通事故迹象\", unless the reviewed evidence covers the full incident window.\n\n## Output Schema\n\nReturn a JSON-compatible result with:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"video\": {},\n  \"visual_timeline\": [\n    {\n      \"time\": \"00:00:12.000\",\n      \"frame_id\": \"frame_000012000ms\",\n      \"observation\": \"Visible subjects, actions, spatial relations, and scene state.\",\n      \"uncertainty\": \"Optional ambiguity note.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"events\": [\n    {\n      \"event_id\": \"EVT_...\",\n      \"event_type\": \"fight | fall_down | traffic_accident | traffic_congestion | crowd_gathering | smoke_or_fire | intrusion | illegal_occupation | other_abnormal_event | unknown\",\n      \"start_time\": \"00:00:10.000\",\n      \"end_time\": \"00:00:18.000\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.0,\n      \"severity\": \"low | medium | high\",\n      \"evidence_frame_ids\": [],\n      \"reason\": \"Concrete visible evidence and uncertainty.\",\n      \"requires_review\": true\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"Short human-readable summary.\",\n  \"warnings\": []\n}\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Do not call legacy rule-based event skills. They have been removed from this bundle.\n- Do not infer off-camera causes.\n- Do not fabricate exact counts when the frame only supports a range.\n","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"read_file","id":"86a7fa18-c416-43d5-945c-091beacd9334","tool_call_id":"call_857292050c754af6bc99d80b","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"技能已加载。现在创建输入文件并执行分析脚本：\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":133,"prompt_tokens":19580,"total_tokens":19713,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":52,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":133},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":19580}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-9ac8d936-a82f-9161-8b03-09dabb1f1512","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1c-32fb-7ea3-87cd-a06fc3f58e4a-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"bash","args":{"command":"ls -la /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 2>&1","description":"检查视频文件是否存在"},"id":"call_178103da008548158153152c","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":19580,"output_tokens":133,"total_tokens":19713,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":52}}},{"content":"ls: cannot access '/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4': No such file or directory","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"bash","id":"032f20c9-8270-4cde-af89-2bed16ce13ff","tool_call_id":"call_178103da008548158153152c","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"视频文件不存在。让我先确认一下上传目录中是否有其他视频文件：\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":142,"prompt_tokens":19700,"total_tokens":19842,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":61,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":142},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":19700}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-f4e16b16-cc05-9e91-ae0b-38dd265cee1f","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e1c-3dc6-74a0-8d6b-a79b6e7f4d88-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"bash","args":{"command":"ls -la /mnt/user-data/uploads/ 2>&1 | head -30","description":"检查上传目录中的文件列表"},"id":"call_9e5d310194d54b4fb603364c","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":19700,"output_tokens":142,"total_tokens":19842,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":61}}}],"artifacts":[],"intent_context":{"intent":"task","original_query":"请分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。","normalized_query":"请分析 /mnt/user data/uploads/does not exist camera 42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。","routing_query":"场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance。场景说明：视频监控、摄像头、监控录像、视频流、实时画面、视频帧、卡口、安防巡检、目标检测、行为识别、事件发现和监控告警分析场景。需要识别参数：视频对象、监控目标、时间范围、输出形式。用户原始问题：我将分析/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4中的打架和摔倒情况，并以时间线形式输出结果","scene":"video_surveillance","scene_name":"视频监控","params":{"视频对象":"/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4","监控目标":"打架、摔倒","输出形式":"时间线"},"scene_mode":"single","scenes":["video_surveillance"],"task_spans":[{"task_span_id":"span_c166bf","text":"请分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。"}],"planning_steps":[{"task_span_id":"span_4e6c54","text":"读取/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4视频文件，校验文件元数据与编码格式，按预设帧率执行流媒体解码与关键帧抽样，输出可供下游模型调用的标准化图像序列与对应时间戳映射表。"},{"task_span_id":"span_c63415","text":"基于视频监控场景的行为识别能力，对抽样帧序列应用人体姿态估计与动作分类模型，聚焦“打架”与“摔倒”两类目标特征进行时空关联分析，设定置信度阈值进行初筛，输出包含事件类型、预估起止时间及置信度分数的候选事件清单。"},{"task_span_id":"span_7e3f0a","text":"依据运动轨迹突变程度与连续帧状态一致性规则，对候选事件清单进行二次交叉研判与噪声过滤，明确异常动作判定的关键指标与排除口径，输出经算法复核确认的高置信度事件区间数据集。"},{"task_span_id":"span_845a2f","text":"将最终确认的事件区间按时间先后逻辑进行序列化编排，整合事件类型、发生时长、画面关键特征摘要及原始视频溯源链接，生成结构化时间线报告供后续业务调度使用。"}],"scene_tasks":[{"sub_task_id":"sub_d4ef0a","scene":"video_surveillance","scene_name":"视频监控","text":"我将分析/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4中的打架和摔倒情况，并以时间线形式输出结果。","params":{"视频对象":"/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4","监控目标":"打架、摔倒","输出形式":"时间线"}}],"sub_tasks":[{"sub_task_id":"sub_d4ef0a","scene":"video_surveillance","scene_name":"视频监控","text":"我将分析/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4中的打架和摔倒情况，并以时间线形式输出结果。","params":{"视频对象":"/mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4","监控目标":"打架、摔倒","输出形式":"时间线"}}],"task_hints":["提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧","提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等","提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口","提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要"],"mentioned_skill_ids":[],"confidence":0.9,"reason":"llm_scene_slot_rewrite","_source_message_key":"id:34ad83b1-a1de-4e51-bbd5-2b2fe8512eb1"},"routing_context":{"route_mode":"scene_filter","trigger":true,"primary_goal":"请分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。","scene_tasks":[{"scene_task_id":"task_001","segment_id":"seg_001","segment_text":"请分析 /mnt/user-data/uploads/does-not-exist-camera-42.mp4 这段监控里有没有打架或摔倒，并给出时间线。","scene":"video_surveillance","input_refs":[],"task_types":[],"selected_skills":[{"id":"analyze-video","role":"primary","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"batch-video-ingestion","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"camera-health-check","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"city-video-intelligence","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"duplicate-event-merge","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"evidence-package-generation","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"evidence-snapshot","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"ffmpeg-utils","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"frame-sampling","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"human-review-routing","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"object-detection","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"object-statistics","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"object-tracking","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"privacy-masking","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"roi-mapping","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"single-video-event-analysis","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"video-embedding-index","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"video-object-analytics","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"video-search","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"video-segment-extraction","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"video-stream-ingestion","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null}],"expected_outputs":[],"depends_on":[]}],"global_selected_skills":["analyze-video","batch-video-ingestion","camera-health-check","city-video-intelligence","duplicate-event-merge","evidence-package-generation","evidence-snapshot","ffmpeg-utils","frame-sampling","human-review-routing","object-detection","object-statistics","object-tracking","privacy-masking","roi-mapping","single-video-event-analysis","video-embedding-index","video-object-analytics","video-search","video-segment-extraction","video-stream-ingestion"],"default_public_skill_ids":[],"global_allowed_tools":[],"confidence":1.0,"route_reason":"SkillRouter disabled; injected all custom skills for detected intent scene as LeadAgent candidate skills","allowed_skills":["analyze-video","batch-video-ingestion","camera-health-check","city-video-intelligence","duplicate-event-merge","evidence-package-generation","evidence-snapshot","ffmpeg-utils","frame-sampling","human-review-routing","object-detection","object-statistics","object-tracking","privacy-masking","roi-mapping","single-video-event-analysis","video-embedding-index